1
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:07,820
No living creature was hurt during
the filming of this series.

2
00:02:26,060 --> 00:02:31,390
Visit our website for more: turkision.com

3
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:47,639
Come on, Alps!

4
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:49,399
Stay together!

5
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:36,519
-Mother!
-Fatma!

6
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,359
Nayman!

7
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:49,319
I kill those who touch my daughter!

8
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:56,439
Fatma, come. Come.

9
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:59,919
-Run. Run without looking back!
-Mother...

10
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,119
Fatma! Listen to me!

11
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:03,439
Run without looking back! Come on!

12
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:26,079
Fatma!

13
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:32,719
Fatma!

14
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:39,599
Fatma!

15
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:42,959
Malhun.. Malhun!

16
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:45,999
Go after Fatma. I'll stay here, come on! Go!

17
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:57,719
Fatma!

18
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:08,679
If we die, we die for this cause..

19
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:13,879
...if we survive we survive for this cause.

20
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:17,759
But we will live today.

21
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:20,839
Allah is the greatest!

22
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:23,359
Allah is the greatest!

23
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:34,719
Kayis are rising against the cruel!

24
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:36,799
The world will bow down before them!

25
00:06:36,960 --> 00:06:39,359
Allah is the greatest!

26
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:28,639
That's how you run.

27
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,759
That's how you will run.

28
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:44,439
-Are you alright?
-I am alright.

29
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:48,279
Allah is the greatest!

30
00:07:48,440 --> 00:08:01,479
Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest!

31
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:06,919
Search around!

32
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:09,999
Dress the wounds of those who are injured.

33
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:12,479
Aykurt...

34
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:15,759
-Are you alright?
-I am alright, my Bey.

35
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:18,399
Samil. Are you alright?

36
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:21,799
I am alright, my Bey.
I am alright.

37
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:24,239
Come on, go check the injured ones.

38
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:34,279
And take him to Yenisehir.

39
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:44,719
That was the vanguard.

40
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:46,479
Their intention..

41
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:49,839
...is to open a road for the ones behind.

42
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:56,519
But... we ruined their move, my Bey.

43
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:58,639
We did.

44
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,679
We did, but...

45
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,359
...they will start attacking us.

46
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:07,319
They can come, my Bey! They can come!

47
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:11,359
We asked for gaza when we turned
these lands into our homeland.

48
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:14,839
We will unite.

49
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:17,119
We will destroy their courage.

50
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:21,239
This land is a homeland for our friends...

51
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:23,839
...and a graveyard for our enemies.

52
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:26,679
Come on Alps. Come on.

53
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:30,319
- In the name of Allah
- Come on, brother.

54
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:48,439
This is the place Boran told us.
But they are not here. Where do you think they are?

55
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:51,759
We'll find them Ayse. We will. Come on, this way.

56
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:55,239
Come on!

57
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:32,319
Fatma!

58
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:35,759
Fatma!

59
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:28,999
Bala mother..

60
00:11:47,920 --> 00:11:49,999
-Mother!
-My daughter!

61
00:11:55,640 --> 00:11:57,159
Hang on!

62
00:11:58,320 --> 00:11:59,799
We are going back!

63
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,319
-My daughter!
-Mother!

64
00:12:11,680 --> 00:12:13,799
Thank Allah.

65
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:17,399
Malhun. Are you alright?

66
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:19,799
We are alright.

67
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:22,999
My Fatma.

68
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:32,999
-You are injured.
-It's not important.

69
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:35,319
Malhun... BoranJ are you alright?

70
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:37,239
Yes, Bala Hatun, I am.

71
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:41,999
Stay here. We will go after them.

72
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:43,959
No. I won't leave you alone.

73
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:46,599
Malhun, you will stay here for your children.

74
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:49,079
Alps! Come on! Go after them!

75
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:51,599
Come on brothers! Come on!

76
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:57,119
Mother... You are bleeding.

77
00:12:57,880 --> 00:13:00,159
It's not deep, don't worry.

78
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:13,239
My Fatma.

79
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:14,159
Bring them to the place I'll tell you.

80
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:17,919
Go. Come Bala..

81
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:21,199
Come. I will bury you all in this forest!

82
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:33,559
Fatma!

83
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,239
May Allah bless you, where are you?

84
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:40,359
You've played enough. Come out, Fatma!

85
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:41,839
Fatma!

86
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:44,079
My daughter, Fatma!

87
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,519
She is not here!

88
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:54,399
-No. We looked everywhere. She is not here.
-Where did she go?

89
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:57,879
She is not in here. If she was, we would find her.

90
00:14:58,160 --> 00:14:59,639
What if she left the mansion?

91
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:03,119
I swear not, Ulgen Hatun. We are not even
letting birds pass, we would see her.

92
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:04,279
The doors are closed.

93
00:15:04,440 --> 00:15:06,519
Where did that child go then?

94
00:15:06,800 --> 00:15:08,199
Mother..

95
00:15:08,320 --> 00:15:10,839
What if she left in Malhun Hatun's carriage?

96
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:14,399
My Allah, protect us.

97
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:17,519
Attention! Osman Bey is coming!

98
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:31,639
Come on!

99
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:35,559
Baysungur, take the wounded
to the healing house.

100
00:15:35,640 --> 00:15:37,279
As you wish, Bey.

101
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:44,719
My little sheep.

102
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:49,479
Quickly, quickly!

103
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:03,079
Where's everyone?

104
00:16:04,640 --> 00:16:05,759
Bey.

105
00:16:06,160 --> 00:16:09,079
You're hurt as well.
Go in and we will take a look.

106
00:16:09,680 --> 00:16:11,359
No, it is not important.

107
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:14,639
It is not important, however,
where is everyone?

108
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:19,799
My Bey, Esrigun Hatun and Boran Alp.

109
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:21,999
They fell in Nayman's trap.

110
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:24,519
Malhun Ha tun and Bala Hatun..

111
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:26,319
Went after them.

112
00:16:26,640 --> 00:16:28,359
What are you saying?

113
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:35,359
Take Halime.

114
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:39,399
Alps, everyone that can hold
a sword comes with me.

115
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:41,599
Dress your wounds.

116
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:43,799
-Let us go.
-Bey.

117
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:45,719
Another thing.

118
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:48,599
VAIIah I don't know where she went, however..

119
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:50,159
Fatma.

120
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:54,399
We can't find her anywhere...
We looked everywhere but...

121
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:57,239
-She's missing.
-What are you saying

122
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:01,719
How is she missing?

123
00:17:02,200 --> 00:17:04,118
How is Fatma missing?

124
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:07,999
What are you doing here?

125
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:12,398
How can you look after such a small child, tell me?

126
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:14,078
What are you doing here?

127
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:18,039
Bey, I never let her out of my sight.

128
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:20,679
She is missing since Malhun Hatun went.

129
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:22,959
I have an idea, however..

130
00:17:23,839 --> 00:17:27,559
Bey, we thought perhaps she went
with the carriage that Malhun Hatun got on.

131
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:45,919
My Fatma..

132
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:52,879
Bey father, don't you miss us?

133
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:54,879
Of course I do.

134
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:59,399
I feel pain at the tip of my nose

135
00:18:00,160 --> 00:18:01,679
whenever I don't see you.

136
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:05,039
You say so, but you always
take my brothers to the battle.

137
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:07,039
You don't take us at all.

138
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:12,679
My dear daughter.

139
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:15,759
My beautiful daughter,
look Halime cannot walk yet.

140
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:19,079
So you need to help her, take care of her.

141
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:26,719
Alps.

142
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:29,199
Everyone to their horses.

143
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:36,399
My heart takes me to enemy's hands.

144
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:44,279
Quickly.

145
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:23,599
You dog.

146
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:32,999
Boran.

147
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:35,839
Are you alright?

148
00:19:36,160 --> 00:19:37,879
I am alright Bala Hatun.

149
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,439
Can you hold on?

150
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:43,559
I can, with Allah's permission.

151
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:46,719
Alright.

152
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:49,239
-Thank you.
-Let us go.

153
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:07,919
This way, tracks lead this way.

154
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:10,479
Alps, sisters, this way.

155
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:11,999
Let us go.

156
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,759
Fatma, what are you doing here?

157
00:20:21,320 --> 00:20:22,759
Why did you come?

158
00:20:23,040 --> 00:20:25,799
We were going to the tribe, how should I know..

159
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:28,359
That you were going into the fight.

160
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:33,359
Are you alright?
Do you have any other wounds?

161
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:35,839
-Are you hurt?
-No.

162
00:20:41,720 --> 00:20:43,239
Osman.

163
00:20:45,680 --> 00:20:48,039
-Malhun.
-Osman.

164
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:51,399
-Father.
-Fatma.

165
00:20:51,840 --> 00:20:53,159
My child.

166
00:20:54,680 --> 00:20:55,759
My dear.

167
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:58,159
-Father.
-My dear.

168
00:20:58,640 --> 00:20:59,999
My dear.

169
00:21:02,080 --> 00:21:05,559
-You're alright?
-I was so scared, father.

170
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:17,959
Malhun.

171
00:21:19,560 --> 00:21:20,959
-Malhun.
-Osman.

172
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:23,879
-Malhun.
-I am alright, don't worry.

173
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:29,159
-Are you alright? Your leg
-I am alright

174
00:21:29,280 --> 00:21:30,919
We are alright.

175
00:21:34,520 --> 00:21:36,759
Osman, Nayman escaped.

176
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:40,279
Catch up to them,
Boran and Bala went after them.

177
00:21:42,360 --> 00:21:45,359
He won't escape, don't worry.

178
00:21:47,080 --> 00:21:49,239
Aktemur, to the horses.

179
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:51,759
Nayman won't escape.

180
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:54,519
We will deal with him now.

181
00:21:55,840 --> 00:21:58,159
This forest will be their grave today, Bey.

182
00:21:58,760 --> 00:22:01,239
It will, quickly now.

183
00:22:07,240 --> 00:22:08,999
You go to Yenisehir.

184
00:22:09,720 --> 00:22:12,479
-Quickly, quickly now.
-Let us go.

185
00:22:54,280 --> 00:22:56,479
Today, all of you are going to die.

186
00:22:56,720 --> 00:23:00,239
It's your blood that is going to
fall on the ground today, Nayman.

187
00:23:00,400 --> 00:23:03,479
We're going to kill you for
a single drop of Fatma's blood.

188
00:23:07,720 --> 00:23:10,839
We're outnumbered.
They drew us into a trap.

189
00:23:11,080 --> 00:23:13,199
Are you afraid, Esrigun Hatun?

190
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:16,999
I'm not worried about myself, but you, Boran Alp.

191
00:23:17,280 --> 00:23:19,359
You have sword wounds all around.

192
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:22,959
They are like just fly bites to me.
Don't worry.

193
00:23:24,960 --> 00:23:26,959
There is no way out of here.

194
00:23:27,120 --> 00:23:29,559
Bless me!

195
00:23:29,600 --> 00:23:31,039
-You have it.
-You have it.

196
00:23:31,040 --> 00:23:32,879
You have it, Ayse!

197
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:36,119
Then... In the name of Allah!

198
00:23:36,120 --> 00:23:38,599
-Allah is the greatest!
-Attack!

199
00:23:39,640 --> 00:23:41,079
Allah is the greatest!

200
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:44,479
Keep Bala's head, though!

201
00:23:44,760 --> 00:23:46,839
We'll send it to Osman.

202
00:23:55,120 --> 00:23:57,479
Well, Osman's hatun..

203
00:23:57,560 --> 00:24:00,199
It seems it's your blood
that will be shed today.

204
00:24:03,960 --> 00:24:05,719
Death is a right for us, Nayman!

205
00:24:05,760 --> 00:24:07,239
It can't fear us.

206
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:10,719
I'll send your head to Osman...

207
00:24:10,840 --> 00:24:13,479
..in silk fabrics.

208
00:25:04,280 --> 00:25:05,599
Osman.

209
00:25:20,800 --> 00:25:21,999
Aktemur.

210
00:25:30,760 --> 00:25:32,199
Nayman!

211
00:25:34,800 --> 00:25:37,239
Today, your head is going to fall!

212
00:25:37,840 --> 00:25:40,599
-Come to me!
-Nokers.

213
00:25:40,920 --> 00:25:42,599
Attack!

214
00:25:45,459 --> 00:25:47,389
Bursa Palace

215
00:25:48,280 --> 00:25:52,159
Lord Valens will make you pay for this.
Where do you think you are going?

216
00:25:52,200 --> 00:25:53,439
To Lefke.

217
00:25:53,560 --> 00:25:55,719
I sent horsemen as a precaution first.

218
00:25:55,920 --> 00:25:58,039
Now I'm going to rule my castle.

219
00:25:58,080 --> 00:26:01,359
We can't leave Gemlik unprotected
while Turks are harassing us.

220
00:26:01,360 --> 00:26:03,999
We're going to leave here.
Lord would understand.

221
00:26:05,440 --> 00:26:09,239
Understand what exactly, Lord?

222
00:26:19,120 --> 00:26:21,439
Why I'm going back to Koyunhisar.

223
00:26:22,280 --> 00:26:25,759
The reason why we are going back
to our castles and citadels, sir.

224
00:26:27,280 --> 00:26:28,799
What's going on here?

225
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:32,399
Sir Valens, bad news reached Bursa before you.

226
00:26:33,680 --> 00:26:34,719
Go ahead.

227
00:26:34,760 --> 00:26:36,759
Osman and his beys are alive.

228
00:26:36,960 --> 00:26:39,039
The vanguard got destroyed.

229
00:26:50,640 --> 00:26:52,679
Osman!

230
00:26:54,160 --> 00:26:57,279
He destroyed Jesus' chosen troop.

231
00:27:00,800 --> 00:27:03,279
I'll be baptized with his blood.

232
00:27:04,560 --> 00:27:06,679
When I kill Osman

233
00:27:06,680 --> 00:27:09,439
...he won't even have a grave to be buried in.

234
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:12,039
I will smash his bones!

235
00:27:15,480 --> 00:27:17,359
And you?

236
00:27:24,160 --> 00:27:27,519
You're going back to your castles like cowards.

237
00:27:31,200 --> 00:27:33,279
Fools.

238
00:27:34,480 --> 00:27:36,359
Now I see better..

239
00:27:36,800 --> 00:27:39,879
...how those shepherds have beaten you...

240
00:27:40,640 --> 00:27:42,559
..for years.

241
00:27:43,040 --> 00:27:45,559
Go hide behind the walls.

242
00:27:46,120 --> 00:27:49,359
Cowards who are afraid of fighting.

243
00:27:50,880 --> 00:27:52,959
We'll fight.

244
00:27:53,640 --> 00:27:56,759
Nayman and I will unite our armies.

245
00:27:57,600 --> 00:28:00,239
We'll take our lands back.

246
00:29:19,960 --> 00:29:21,679
You attacked..

247
00:29:22,200 --> 00:29:24,679
...my house and children, huh?

248
00:29:29,440 --> 00:29:31,599
You think I'll leave you like this?

249
00:29:31,840 --> 00:29:34,599
Come here. I will..

250
00:29:35,080 --> 00:29:37,959
I will... I will..

251
00:29:38,240 --> 00:29:41,239
I will take your everything.

252
00:29:41,320 --> 00:29:45,079
You will have only your life left.

253
00:29:51,600 --> 00:29:53,679
Come.

254
00:29:54,360 --> 00:29:57,159
Come here. Come.

255
00:30:04,520 --> 00:30:06,799
You will pay for what you did.

256
00:30:09,360 --> 00:30:11,599
Come.

257
00:30:12,200 --> 00:30:14,319
Get up! Get up!

258
00:30:16,160 --> 00:30:19,039
You will pay.

259
00:30:19,160 --> 00:30:20,839
Get up!

260
00:30:37,160 --> 00:30:40,159
I'm going to survive this too.

261
00:30:41,680 --> 00:30:44,999
Then I will spit on you.

262
00:30:47,360 --> 00:30:49,439
Where are you going to go, ha?

263
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:51,879
Where are you going to go?

264
00:30:53,400 --> 00:30:55,919
You think I'll leave you?

265
00:30:56,400 --> 00:30:58,239
You can't go anywhere!

266
00:31:07,400 --> 00:31:09,439
Which commanders will turn against...

267
00:31:09,560 --> 00:31:11,599
..after you fall?

268
00:31:11,800 --> 00:31:14,079
You'll give me all the names.

269
00:31:15,880 --> 00:31:20,079
Come here.

270
00:31:20,280 --> 00:31:23,199
All of them will fight to avenge me.

271
00:31:23,560 --> 00:31:26,759
But you can't kill me.

272
00:31:26,880 --> 00:31:28,319
Osman..

273
00:31:38,480 --> 00:31:43,279
Esrigun won't let that happen.

274
00:31:52,000 --> 00:31:53,999
You say so, huh?

275
00:31:54,920 --> 00:31:56,719
You say so?

276
00:31:59,960 --> 00:32:01,839
Now..

277
00:32:05,880 --> 00:32:07,999
Stand up.

278
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:10,839
Here..

279
00:32:11,120 --> 00:32:14,879
I'm both the Bey and the state.

280
00:32:15,760 --> 00:32:18,679
And only I can decide...

281
00:32:20,160 --> 00:32:22,519
...who is going to die.

282
00:32:30,840 --> 00:32:33,839
Now give me the names of the commanders.

283
00:32:36,360 --> 00:32:38,079
Come on!

284
00:32:38,280 --> 00:32:41,799
A great army...

285
00:32:42,520 --> 00:32:44,119
will come

286
00:32:44,440 --> 00:32:47,599
after you.

287
00:32:47,800 --> 00:32:50,159
Those who hate Gazan.

288
00:32:51,160 --> 00:32:54,799
Even if I die, they will keep fighting...

289
00:32:55,040 --> 00:32:57,999
...and make this place a homeland for them.

290
00:33:08,880 --> 00:33:10,359
Come.

291
00:33:12,080 --> 00:33:15,279
I'll let them know too, don't worry.

292
00:33:15,480 --> 00:33:19,679
I'll bury the one who sets eye on my lands
under the ground of my lands.

293
00:33:20,680 --> 00:33:23,399
Bury them Osman, bury them.

294
00:33:25,200 --> 00:33:27,279
When I get back from Tebriz,

295
00:33:27,640 --> 00:33:31,279
I'll bury you too.

296
00:33:33,400 --> 00:33:35,879
Do you think I'll let you go?

297
00:33:36,800 --> 00:33:39,239
You can't go anywhere.

298
00:33:41,640 --> 00:33:43,599
Osman Bey.

299
00:33:46,280 --> 00:33:48,599
Nayman's head is Gazan Khan's right.

300
00:33:51,720 --> 00:33:54,559
He will be taken to Tebriz with a solid troop.

301
00:33:55,120 --> 00:33:57,759
Gazan Khan wants to receive Nayman alive.

302
00:34:31,679 --> 00:34:33,478
Osman Bey.

303
00:34:34,199 --> 00:34:35,518
I'm not talking in vain.

304
00:34:36,320 --> 00:34:40,158
You will follow the orders of Gazan Khan
who saved you from such chaos.

305
00:34:40,960 --> 00:34:43,279
You do not deserve to take Nayman's head.

306
00:35:00,240 --> 00:35:02,999
As Esrigun Hatun wishes.

307
00:35:08,080 --> 00:35:09,439
Come here Ayaz.

308
00:35:18,600 --> 00:35:20,919
-Yes my Bey.
-Alps!

309
00:35:21,680 --> 00:35:24,159
You will go to Nayman's outpost.

310
00:35:24,840 --> 00:35:26,799
Guards will stay there.

311
00:35:27,280 --> 00:35:29,479
Don't let anyone get inside.

312
00:35:41,080 --> 00:35:43,679
We will go to Yenisehir.

313
00:35:55,160 --> 00:35:57,239
Come on, get him up.

314
00:36:03,480 --> 00:36:04,759
Folks

315
00:36:05,320 --> 00:36:08,719
Don't forget,
these two great armies will unite.

316
00:36:18,720 --> 00:36:20,199
Sir.

317
00:36:20,600 --> 00:36:23,879
Sir, Osman cornered Nayman.

318
00:36:24,800 --> 00:36:26,559
He will capture him soon.

319
00:36:29,120 --> 00:36:31,599
Capturing Nayman won't be enough for Osman.

320
00:36:31,960 --> 00:36:34,559
He will want more as his ancestors.

321
00:36:35,200 --> 00:36:38,479
Osman wants to take our castles.

322
00:36:38,720 --> 00:36:41,959
We should go to our castles and take precautions.

323
00:36:43,400 --> 00:36:45,319
Lords!

324
00:36:49,160 --> 00:36:51,679
We will no longer hide behind the walls

325
00:36:52,200 --> 00:36:54,399
and defend them!

326
00:36:55,600 --> 00:36:57,599
We will attack.

327
00:36:59,080 --> 00:37:02,079
We will destroy Turks in a battlefield.

328
00:37:02,480 --> 00:37:05,799
How can we do it without Nayman's army, Lord Valens?

329
00:37:08,760 --> 00:37:10,919
I will go to Constantinople.

330
00:37:12,160 --> 00:37:16,159
I will ask for his army from Emperor Andronikos.

331
00:37:16,640 --> 00:37:20,279
If we save Nayman,
we will not need Emperor's support.

332
00:37:22,280 --> 00:37:26,199
No one can save Nayman from Osman anymore.

333
00:37:29,280 --> 00:37:31,519
Nayman is a dead man.

334
00:37:33,080 --> 00:37:37,799
Soon, I'll take Osman's life, his people

335
00:37:39,280 --> 00:37:41,039
I'll take everything from him.

336
00:37:42,680 --> 00:37:45,519
Leo, get the horses ready.

337
00:37:56,600 --> 00:37:58,279
Move!

338
00:37:59,720 --> 00:38:00,999
Move!

339
00:38:01,400 --> 00:38:04,719
-Look at him!
-Move.

340
00:38:07,920 --> 00:38:09,679
Move.

341
00:38:12,040 --> 00:38:14,719
Move! Come on!

342
00:38:16,160 --> 00:38:17,359
Move!

343
00:39:04,160 --> 00:39:08,119
I'll kill them all.

344
00:39:14,680 --> 00:39:16,279
Infidel!

345
00:39:18,040 --> 00:39:20,319
I'll kill them all.

346
00:39:29,480 --> 00:39:31,719
-Punish him!
-Just wait.

347
00:39:32,160 --> 00:39:34,319
Just wait, hang on.

348
00:39:50,520 --> 00:39:52,879
Comparison to what you did,

349
00:39:55,000 --> 00:39:57,319
this is nothing.

350
00:39:59,640 --> 00:40:01,839
Wait.

351
00:40:04,240 --> 00:40:06,039
I will not let you

352
00:40:06,880 --> 00:40:09,159
walk towards your death.

353
00:40:18,320 --> 00:40:19,879
Open up.

354
00:40:33,640 --> 00:40:35,039
What's this Osman Bey?

355
00:40:35,200 --> 00:40:37,639
Everyone gets what they deserve.

356
00:41:25,200 --> 00:41:27,079
Come on.

357
00:41:27,760 --> 00:41:29,519
Come to your end.

358
00:41:31,520 --> 00:41:33,199
Come.

359
00:42:03,240 --> 00:42:04,559
Come here.

360
00:42:09,080 --> 00:42:10,919
Walk.

361
00:42:14,800 --> 00:42:16,479
Move.

362
00:42:28,640 --> 00:42:30,239
Folks!

363
00:42:31,240 --> 00:42:32,679
Here

364
00:42:35,160 --> 00:42:37,199
here's the dastard Nayman,

365
00:42:38,040 --> 00:42:39,919
who is the head of

366
00:42:41,680 --> 00:42:44,399
many oppressions and evil tricks.

367
00:42:48,120 --> 00:42:49,239
Now

368
00:42:50,200 --> 00:42:52,599
Esrigun Hatun says that

369
00:42:55,160 --> 00:42:56,919
Gazan Khan

370
00:42:57,680 --> 00:42:59,799
deserves to take his head.

371
00:43:03,480 --> 00:43:07,639
But I say that the best enemy

372
00:43:09,400 --> 00:43:11,479
is the one who is under the ground.

373
00:43:16,800 --> 00:43:19,239
He tortured my people.

374
00:43:20,440 --> 00:43:23,159
He shed blood of my people.

375
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:26,999
From now on

376
00:43:32,560 --> 00:43:34,439
his blood

377
00:43:36,480 --> 00:43:38,479
is our right.

378
00:43:43,800 --> 00:43:47,319
The price of what you're doing
will be very heavy, Osman Bey.

379
00:43:47,320 --> 00:43:48,959
Nayman will get to Tebriz.

380
00:43:49,320 --> 00:43:51,719
Gazan Khan will punish him.

381
00:43:52,320 --> 00:43:54,999
No, no.

382
00:43:58,480 --> 00:44:02,159
I will never let him get away from me again.

383
00:44:07,200 --> 00:44:09,839
The only thing that will go to Gazan Khan

384
00:44:11,640 --> 00:44:13,799
will be this dastard's head.

385
00:44:15,880 --> 00:44:17,559
My death

386
00:44:18,280 --> 00:44:21,399
will cause vengeance to emerge, Osman.

387
00:44:22,280 --> 00:44:24,799
Holy war is bigger than vengeance.

388
00:44:25,800 --> 00:44:28,799
Whoever sets eyes on our lands

389
00:44:30,120 --> 00:44:32,479
will be ruined.

390
00:44:43,000 --> 00:44:44,639
Your head

391
00:44:46,880 --> 00:44:49,359
will be a warning for them.

392
00:44:52,400 --> 00:44:54,479
Osman Bey.

393
00:45:02,360 --> 00:45:04,359
Gok Teng

394
00:45:05,240 --> 00:45:07,519
I fought for you.

395
00:45:08,440 --> 00:45:10,479
I will die for you.

396
00:45:12,280 --> 00:45:13,599
But

397
00:45:17,160 --> 00:45:18,839
everything

398
00:45:20,880 --> 00:45:22,959
will be done in order.

399
00:45:30,120 --> 00:45:32,199
Your time has come.

400
00:45:56,400 --> 00:45:58,399
What did you do Osman Bey?

401
00:46:00,600 --> 00:46:02,279
I did what was necessary.

402
00:46:03,240 --> 00:46:05,359
Without even thinking about it.

403
00:46:06,000 --> 00:46:07,959
You hunted Gazan Khan's prey.

404
00:46:08,080 --> 00:46:09,959
How are you going to answer him?

405
00:46:10,200 --> 00:46:13,399
The prey does not belong
to the one who laid his eyes on it...

406
00:46:13,800 --> 00:46:15,559
...but to the one who beheads it.

407
00:46:16,800 --> 00:46:18,719
Tell this to Gazan Khan.

408
00:46:30,920 --> 00:46:33,359
Boran. Bring that head.

409
00:46:36,480 --> 00:46:38,719
Come here.

410
00:46:43,120 --> 00:46:44,599
Here..

411
00:46:46,840 --> 00:46:48,999
...another cruel's head fell down.

412
00:46:54,520 --> 00:46:56,799
But there are still many of them!

413
00:46:58,240 --> 00:47:01,039
They are all waiting for us in ambush.

414
00:47:01,760 --> 00:47:02,719
Now..

415
00:47:03,400 --> 00:47:06,679
...we will attack before they attack.

416
00:47:08,880 --> 00:47:10,759
Now the conquests won't stop.

417
00:47:11,080 --> 00:47:14,239
Alps! Send news to all houses...

418
00:47:14,880 --> 00:47:18,439
...to all tribes, to all places!

419
00:47:20,200 --> 00:47:22,639
All valiants who can hold swords...

420
00:47:24,880 --> 00:47:26,679
..will stand next to us.

421
00:47:26,720 --> 00:47:28,839
Yes my Bey!

422
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:32,439
Turks' sanjaks...

423
00:47:33,520 --> 00:47:36,359
...will gather under one sanjak now.

424
00:47:45,120 --> 00:47:47,399
And we will come for the cruel!

425
00:47:47,920 --> 00:47:52,319
Allah is the greatest!

426
00:47:52,320 --> 00:47:56,839
Allah is the greatest!

427
00:47:56,960 --> 00:47:58,599
Allah is the greatest!

428
00:47:58,680 --> 00:48:01,799
Allah is the greatest!

429
00:48:01,880 --> 00:48:05,559
Long live Osman Bey!

430
00:48:05,640 --> 00:48:13,079
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

431
00:48:13,080 --> 00:48:15,079
Long live Osman Bey!

432
00:48:30,080 --> 00:48:33,239
Stop, wait a second brother.

433
00:48:42,000 --> 00:48:43,879
What happened brother?

434
00:48:45,880 --> 00:48:48,319
You look like a groom.

435
00:48:50,160 --> 00:48:52,119
Is there something we don't know?

436
00:48:54,160 --> 00:48:56,759
What groom are you talking about, brother?

437
00:48:56,960 --> 00:48:58,199
You are the groom.

438
00:48:58,880 --> 00:49:01,959
O, you are the one
who looks too much of a groom.

439
00:49:03,400 --> 00:49:05,639
He thinks everyone is like him.

440
00:49:07,640 --> 00:49:09,119
No, brother.

441
00:49:09,560 --> 00:49:13,359
There is something different about you. Cerkutay is right.

442
00:49:16,840 --> 00:49:18,039
Brother, what can I do?

443
00:49:18,160 --> 00:49:23,319
Should I wear cheap clothes and
look careless in front of those people, Konur?

444
00:49:24,880 --> 00:49:27,799
No, sure. Look at yourself.

445
00:49:28,200 --> 00:49:30,639
You are a man who looks like a mountain.

446
00:49:30,760 --> 00:49:34,359
You might become a groom of a Khan anytime.

447
00:49:36,400 --> 00:49:39,679
I can teach you Mongolian once in a while, Boran.

448
00:49:41,640 --> 00:49:43,519
You might need it.

449
00:49:48,120 --> 00:49:50,719
Brother, you are making fun of me.

450
00:49:51,520 --> 00:49:54,959
Come on. Come on, brother. My Bey is waiting for us.

451
00:49:56,160 --> 00:49:57,839
Come on. Go.

452
00:49:58,160 --> 00:49:59,839
Our Bey is waiting for us...

453
00:50:00,440 --> 00:50:03,759
...but there must be someone else waiting for you. Right?

454
00:50:08,720 --> 00:50:10,599
You really had fun here, brothers.

455
00:50:11,640 --> 00:50:14,239
-Confess.
-Come on.

456
00:50:14,680 --> 00:50:17,959
Come on, Cerkutay. Move. Move.

457
00:50:22,080 --> 00:50:23,919
Brother, move!

458
00:50:24,360 --> 00:50:26,479
Brother... Aren't you going to tell us...

459
00:50:27,160 --> 00:50:29,599
...how you saved Esrigun Hatun.

460
00:50:32,960 --> 00:50:33,999
So?

461
00:50:34,320 --> 00:50:38,319
Brothers... May Allah let me end up
at the edge of Dark Midwife's staff.

462
00:50:41,360 --> 00:50:44,119
At least it's better than
being a prey in your chat!

463
00:50:44,360 --> 00:50:47,999
Please. The grass looks greener on the other side.

464
00:50:51,400 --> 00:50:53,159
Come on, my Bey is waiting.

465
00:50:53,680 --> 00:50:56,679
Come on! Come on brothers!

466
00:51:14,560 --> 00:51:18,359
Brother, we are going to attend the meeting, you'll come later.

467
00:51:18,400 --> 00:51:20,919
We are going, you will attend later.

468
00:51:21,160 --> 00:51:24,639
Brother, we are going to attend the meeting, you'll come later.

469
00:51:31,080 --> 00:51:33,039
How is your wound, Boran Alp?

470
00:51:34,880 --> 00:51:36,519
I am alright, thanks to Allah.

471
00:51:37,080 --> 00:51:39,439
I've experienced worse ones, Esrigun Hatun.

472
00:51:41,480 --> 00:51:45,399
I... could not thank you
since I was dealing with...

473
00:51:46,440 --> 00:51:48,319
...so many things.

474
00:51:50,240 --> 00:51:52,239
It's not a problem, Esrigun Hatun.

475
00:51:52,640 --> 00:51:54,959
I just did my duty.

476
00:51:55,400 --> 00:51:58,839
No. You did more than your duty.

477
00:52:01,840 --> 00:52:03,919
I owe you my life now.

478
00:52:05,160 --> 00:52:06,719
No, Esrigun Hatun. No.

479
00:52:07,560 --> 00:52:09,399
You do not owe me.

480
00:52:11,000 --> 00:52:13,999
Besides, I did what I was told.

481
00:52:21,360 --> 00:52:22,559
This is yours.

482
00:52:31,280 --> 00:52:33,719
No, Esrigun Hatun. I cannot accept this.

483
00:52:34,680 --> 00:52:36,239
It's my gift, Boran Alp.

484
00:52:36,440 --> 00:52:38,679
How can one return gifts?

485
00:52:59,560 --> 00:53:01,679
Thank you.
Live long.

486
00:53:13,800 --> 00:53:15,679
You protected me...

487
00:53:16,200 --> 00:53:18,599
...and may this protect you when you feel weak.

488
00:53:34,440 --> 00:53:37,159
My Bey is waiting for me. I should go to him.

489
00:53:38,600 --> 00:53:40,119
Thank you.

490
00:53:41,360 --> 00:53:42,639
Thank you.

491
00:54:04,840 --> 00:54:08,559
I... am the littlest son of the dynasty...

492
00:54:10,240 --> 00:54:12,319
...Valens Leon.

493
00:54:13,840 --> 00:54:16,319
I was born as a Mouzalon.

494
00:54:17,800 --> 00:54:21,199
And I've fought for years as a Mouzalon.

495
00:54:22,960 --> 00:54:26,559
My family made great armies kneel.

496
00:54:28,360 --> 00:54:31,239
They defeated people who were called "invincible".

497
00:54:34,720 --> 00:54:38,519
It was all for you, Holy Jesus.

498
00:54:40,920 --> 00:54:43,079
You tamed me.

499
00:54:46,560 --> 00:54:49,839
They took the fearsome Mouzalon..

500
00:54:53,160 --> 00:54:56,199
And made me Lord Valens.

501
00:55:01,000 --> 00:55:02,359
Priest.

502
00:55:04,320 --> 00:55:06,759
I want to be re-baptised.

503
00:55:08,640 --> 00:55:10,719
I want to reincarnate..

504
00:55:12,040 --> 00:55:14,559
As Commander Mouzalon.

505
00:55:17,720 --> 00:55:19,479
Come, my son.

506
00:55:27,200 --> 00:55:29,089
Do you believe that..

507
00:55:29,170 --> 00:55:32,239
Jesus is your saviour and your God?

508
00:55:33,720 --> 00:55:34,839
Yes.

509
00:55:36,040 --> 00:55:39,519
May this holy water reincarnate you, Mouzalon.

510
00:55:41,080 --> 00:55:43,729
I baptise you, in the name of..

511
00:55:43,780 --> 00:55:48,359
Our God, Jesus Christ and
The Holy Spirit.

512
00:55:53,120 --> 00:55:54,599
Amen.

513
00:55:58,480 --> 00:56:00,119
Jesus Christ.

514
00:56:02,080 --> 00:56:03,479
Bless me.

515
00:56:05,680 --> 00:56:09,239
Bless me, so I can
spill the blood of Turks.

516
00:56:22,120 --> 00:56:24,359
I am reborn as..

517
00:56:27,040 --> 00:56:29,199
Commander Mouzalon.

518
00:56:39,360 --> 00:56:40,839
My dear daughter.

519
00:56:41,200 --> 00:56:43,719
Festival of my heart.

520
00:56:44,120 --> 00:56:47,239
What if something happened to you?
What would I do then?

521
00:56:47,440 --> 00:56:49,319
Could I live without you?

522
00:56:50,440 --> 00:56:52,999
What, my new sibling would come.

523
00:56:54,040 --> 00:56:57,159
Where are my shoes anyway?

524
00:56:57,320 --> 00:56:59,799
Did you throw them away so suddenly?

525
00:57:00,320 --> 00:57:02,919
Of course not.

526
00:57:06,120 --> 00:57:07,839
Are you..

527
00:57:08,920 --> 00:57:10,959
Talking about these bychance?

528
00:57:12,280 --> 00:57:14,799
Yes, I am talking about those, Osman Bey.

529
00:57:15,000 --> 00:57:17,159
Did you get them from the roof?

530
00:57:17,840 --> 00:57:19,999
No, not roof.

531
00:57:24,360 --> 00:57:26,759
I had them made for you.

532
00:57:29,040 --> 00:57:30,559
However..

533
00:57:30,880 --> 00:57:33,719
If you don't come have dinner with me..

534
00:57:35,880 --> 00:57:38,239
I won't give these to you.

535
00:57:42,680 --> 00:57:45,759
Good, then my growing sibling can wear them.

536
00:57:46,280 --> 00:57:48,159
I am not hungry anyway.

537
00:57:48,680 --> 00:57:50,479
Look at you.

538
00:57:54,360 --> 00:57:56,479
You two keep talking.

539
00:57:56,520 --> 00:58:00,959
And I will have a look at the table.
Maybe Fatma would be hungry by then.

540
00:58:56,200 --> 00:58:58,319
My beautiful dear.

541
00:59:01,720 --> 00:59:04,239
My beauty.

542
00:59:05,520 --> 00:59:06,999
Look at you.

543
00:59:07,520 --> 00:59:09,799
What if something happened to you?

544
00:59:10,160 --> 00:59:12,359
What if I never saw you again?

545
00:59:12,840 --> 00:59:14,919
Then what would I had done, tell me?

546
00:59:15,240 --> 00:59:18,759
You already don't see me Osman Bey,
you only see your Alps.

547
00:59:18,880 --> 00:59:20,479
You only see Iltutan.

548
00:59:20,600 --> 00:59:22,919
Even you see your enemies more than us.

549
00:59:23,520 --> 00:59:26,479
You either go to battle or work for battle.

550
00:59:26,640 --> 00:59:29,959
Will you be always Osman Bey?
When will you be our Bey Father?

551
00:59:32,600 --> 00:59:34,279
Come here.

552
00:59:38,000 --> 00:59:39,639
I am your father.

553
00:59:41,080 --> 00:59:42,919
Of course I am your father.

554
00:59:45,200 --> 00:59:47,559
I am Osman Bey sometimes..

555
00:59:48,800 --> 00:59:51,039
And your Bey Father the other times.

556
00:59:55,040 --> 00:59:56,679
I was very scared father.

557
00:59:58,000 --> 00:59:59,239
I was very scared.

558
01:00:04,440 --> 01:00:07,079
I want to see my father more.

559
01:00:08,320 --> 01:00:09,879
My dear.

560
01:00:12,320 --> 01:00:13,679
My dear.

561
01:00:15,880 --> 01:00:18,399
Do you know why you can't see me?

562
01:00:23,320 --> 01:00:26,799
So that your children can born to a strong state.

563
01:00:28,480 --> 01:00:32,879
Don't you think that
I want to see you every second?

564
01:00:35,000 --> 01:00:36,159
However..

565
01:00:37,400 --> 01:00:40,119
However, now this well.

566
01:00:42,960 --> 01:00:44,839
We do not live for ourselves.

567
01:00:45,200 --> 01:00:48,399
Our only concern is the Divine Word.

568
01:00:48,400 --> 01:00:51,359
Our fight is for Islam Nation.

569
01:00:51,880 --> 01:00:53,679
In this road..

570
01:00:53,800 --> 01:00:56,799
The longing we have for our home and children..

571
01:00:57,960 --> 01:00:59,999
Is our greatest challenge.

572
01:01:02,440 --> 01:01:04,199
Do you also miss us?

573
01:01:06,280 --> 01:01:08,159
Of course I do.

574
01:01:11,160 --> 01:01:13,239
Of course.

575
01:01:22,440 --> 01:01:23,999
However..

576
01:01:25,120 --> 01:01:28,119
I don't think you miss me.
Because if you did..

577
01:01:29,800 --> 01:01:31,719
You would've come to dinner with me.

578
01:01:59,480 --> 01:02:01,839
Let's go before food gets cold, Bey Father.

579
01:02:02,720 --> 01:02:05,119
My dear, that's it.

580
01:02:05,840 --> 01:02:08,079
That's it.

581
01:02:12,520 --> 01:02:13,839
Let us go.

582
01:02:14,240 --> 01:02:15,999
Let us go.

583
01:02:18,600 --> 01:02:19,919
My dear Fatma.

584
01:02:20,160 --> 01:02:22,799
Since she found her father she shows coyness.

585
01:02:25,480 --> 01:02:27,279
She does of course.

586
01:02:27,560 --> 01:02:31,479
Did you already forget
what she did until Halime came?

587
01:02:31,760 --> 01:02:33,439
Of course not.

588
01:02:33,920 --> 01:02:37,039
However, when Halime was seen
all went out to be well.

589
01:02:37,440 --> 01:02:40,679
These are sweet coyness,
right Halime?

590
01:02:41,400 --> 01:02:43,119
Thank Allah.

591
01:02:43,480 --> 01:02:45,479
She is very beautiful, praise be.

592
01:02:45,920 --> 01:02:47,599
May her destiny is well also.

593
01:02:47,880 --> 01:02:50,119
-Amen.
-Amen.

594
01:02:51,520 --> 01:02:52,759
Amen.

595
01:03:11,160 --> 01:03:13,959
May the same happen to you soon as well,
Esrigun Hatun.

596
01:03:17,680 --> 01:03:20,119
However, you should be quick.

597
01:03:28,000 --> 01:03:31,119
Brothers will be fine tomorrow,
right Dark Midwife?

598
01:03:31,120 --> 01:03:35,559
My mother made soup with her own hands.

599
01:03:35,560 --> 01:03:38,039
Of course they will be alright, brother.

600
01:03:38,040 --> 01:03:40,759
My mother's hands heal.

601
01:03:41,720 --> 01:03:43,519
Oh lunatic boy, oh!

602
01:03:43,800 --> 01:03:45,959
You have a gift for gab.

603
01:03:46,480 --> 01:03:48,399
You are something else!

604
01:03:50,360 --> 01:03:52,759
He, Dark Midwife...

605
01:03:53,360 --> 01:03:56,239
He is a dark horse, my brother.

606
01:03:57,880 --> 01:03:59,759
He may be a dark horse..

607
01:04:00,080 --> 01:04:02,999
But he is mine now.

608
01:04:08,600 --> 01:04:10,559
Stop messing with my brother.

609
01:04:11,240 --> 01:04:13,719
He has just became a groom.

610
01:04:21,680 --> 01:04:23,679
Peace be upon you.

611
01:04:23,880 --> 01:04:25,799
Peace be upon you too.

612
01:04:26,200 --> 01:04:27,919
Peace be upon you too.

613
01:04:28,680 --> 01:04:30,719
Praise be, praise be!

614
01:04:31,480 --> 01:04:33,519
May your chat be plenteous.

615
01:04:34,800 --> 01:04:36,079
My little lamb.

616
01:04:37,400 --> 01:04:38,839
Come.

617
01:04:40,280 --> 01:04:41,919
Come here.

618
01:04:44,240 --> 01:04:47,559
-Through here.
-Come my beautiful daughter.

619
01:04:50,760 --> 01:04:52,759
You may sit.

620
01:04:59,640 --> 01:05:02,519
-Another enemy head fell off my Bey.
-That's right.

621
01:05:03,640 --> 01:05:06,119
We cut another enemy's head as well.

622
01:05:06,320 --> 01:05:09,359
But there are thousands more ahead.

623
01:05:16,800 --> 01:05:18,079
Fatma Sultan.

624
01:05:19,040 --> 01:05:22,119
It is not the time to talk about battle.

625
01:05:23,800 --> 01:05:25,399
Now Osman Bey is gone

626
01:05:25,560 --> 01:05:27,559
Father Osman is here right, father?

627
01:05:27,680 --> 01:05:28,959
That's right.

628
01:05:29,680 --> 01:05:31,319
That's right.

629
01:05:33,120 --> 01:05:34,159
My Halime.

630
01:05:34,320 --> 01:05:37,319
Come here now.

631
01:05:39,880 --> 01:05:43,479
What's that? Are you going to
grow up and go to battle?

632
01:05:45,320 --> 01:05:47,719
No. Come on now.

633
01:05:48,200 --> 01:05:50,719
Get into the middle with your spoon.

634
01:05:51,800 --> 01:05:54,919
Come on, come on walk.

635
01:05:55,360 --> 01:05:57,359
Come on, before battle...

636
01:06:11,360 --> 01:06:14,079
So you almost went to the battle, is that so?

637
01:06:14,800 --> 01:06:17,719
But you are too little for battle now.

638
01:06:18,000 --> 01:06:19,359
My Halime, come here.

639
01:06:19,440 --> 01:06:22,439
No, don't. I did it, but you stay away from it sister.

640
01:06:22,880 --> 01:06:24,639
We're not ready for battle yet.

641
01:06:24,840 --> 01:06:27,079
I'm glad that Ulgen sister held Halime.

642
01:06:27,400 --> 01:06:30,599
I wish I had been more careful and
I had caught you too Fatma.

643
01:06:31,480 --> 01:06:33,959
Don't play games without my knowledge again.

644
01:06:34,080 --> 01:06:35,879
I will not tell anyone, all right?

645
01:06:36,000 --> 01:06:38,959
I said tawba, I'd
never do that again.

646
01:06:39,440 --> 01:06:41,519
It's not like the trainings at all.

647
01:06:41,520 --> 01:06:43,439
Of course it's not, my angel daughter.

648
01:06:43,440 --> 01:06:46,039
In battle, you have your enemies against you,

649
01:06:46,040 --> 01:06:47,999
in training, you have your brothers.

650
01:06:48,520 --> 01:06:51,239
My brothers let me breathe

651
01:06:51,720 --> 01:06:55,639
but they would not wait for me
to breathe in battle, right?

652
01:06:55,840 --> 01:06:57,999
They would not, Fatma.

653
01:06:58,440 --> 01:07:01,599
That is why you need to train
yourself in a great way.

654
01:07:02,360 --> 01:07:05,199
Right. Oh my beautiful daughter.

655
01:07:06,400 --> 01:07:07,599
Halime.

656
01:07:09,960 --> 01:07:12,679
Come here, come.

657
01:07:13,080 --> 01:07:16,919
Come here. Come here.

658
01:07:18,320 --> 01:07:20,439
Let's eat, enjoy your meal.

659
01:07:20,600 --> 01:07:21,639
My Bala.

660
01:07:22,240 --> 01:07:24,919
Give her to me my Bey. Come here daughter.

661
01:07:25,800 --> 01:07:27,999
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate.

662
01:07:49,920 --> 01:07:51,919
Any news from Baysungur?

663
01:07:52,360 --> 01:07:54,559
We got news my Bey he want to take it.

664
01:07:58,160 --> 01:08:00,279
Very well.

665
01:08:01,920 --> 01:08:04,359
So, Dark Midwife, tell me

666
01:08:04,760 --> 01:08:06,839
whose turn is it for wedding?

667
01:08:07,360 --> 01:08:09,319
Is there anyone on your mind?

668
01:08:11,720 --> 01:08:14,439
There is my Bey, there is.

669
01:08:15,120 --> 01:08:17,038
There is someone in my mind.

670
01:08:21,880 --> 01:08:23,639
However

671
01:08:27,560 --> 01:08:29,999
it's too soon right now.

672
01:08:40,319 --> 01:08:42,278
Well done brother.

673
01:08:42,600 --> 01:08:44,479
Well done.

674
01:08:44,920 --> 01:08:48,078
Start collecting gold right now.

675
01:08:48,840 --> 01:08:51,158
It is too hard to collect them later on.

676
01:08:54,279 --> 01:08:56,158
Cerkutay.

677
01:08:57,319 --> 01:09:00,198
You look naive, but you're such a rascal.

678
01:09:14,319 --> 01:09:15,439
May I come in, my Bey?

679
01:09:16,920 --> 01:09:18,919
Come in Baysungu

680
01:09:27,000 --> 01:09:29,639
My Bey, we got a message from Marthaleus.

681
01:09:34,840 --> 01:09:38,318
Osman Bey, Lord Valens came to Constantinople.

682
01:09:38,760 --> 01:09:41,599
I'm following his every step as you ordered.

683
01:09:52,840 --> 01:09:54,278
Fatma.

684
01:09:56,120 --> 01:09:59,519
It's time for Bey Osman.

685
01:10:07,520 --> 01:10:10,639
Alps, inform Beys...

686
01:10:11,120 --> 01:10:14,319
-We'll have the council.
-As you order, my Bey.

687
01:10:40,200 --> 01:10:42,159
Lord Valens, welcome.

688
01:10:42,240 --> 01:10:44,519
Emperor didn't know you would come.

689
01:10:44,560 --> 01:10:48,159
-If you...
-Unexpected things are happening to me too!

690
01:10:48,440 --> 01:10:49,799
We are losing...

691
01:10:49,880 --> 01:10:53,039
...our soldiers, lands and Byzantine.

692
01:10:53,320 --> 01:10:55,199
I have no time to lose.

693
01:10:55,600 --> 01:10:57,919
Let Emperor know!

694
01:10:58,680 --> 01:11:00,959
Sure, Lord Valens.

695
01:11:01,080 --> 01:11:02,719
Not Valens..

696
01:11:02,960 --> 01:11:05,759
...but Mouzalon, the Butcher of Turks is here.

697
01:11:10,600 --> 01:11:13,119
My Bey, beys are here.

698
01:11:13,280 --> 01:11:15,039
May they come in?

699
01:11:15,320 --> 01:11:18,079
Let them in.

700
01:11:19,360 --> 01:11:21,519
Come in, beys.

701
01:11:27,280 --> 01:11:29,399
Welcome.

702
01:11:36,200 --> 01:11:37,999
Tell me.

703
01:11:38,600 --> 01:11:42,519
What's the situation in the lands
the wolf set his eyes on?

704
01:11:43,920 --> 01:11:45,479
My Bey.

705
01:11:45,840 --> 01:11:48,479
Forgive me, but...

706
01:11:49,640 --> 01:11:51,719
For this at this time?

707
01:11:51,960 --> 01:11:54,039
Well, be patient.

708
01:11:54,680 --> 01:11:56,879
Let's speak of the good first.

709
01:11:57,360 --> 01:11:59,119
We will..

710
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:02,479
..talk about the bad too.

711
01:12:05,680 --> 01:12:06,959
Uraz Bey, speak.

712
01:12:07,480 --> 01:12:10,199
They're fortifying the defense in Kestel Castle.

713
01:12:10,280 --> 01:12:13,319
They were sure the troop
that had come would hit us.

714
01:12:13,680 --> 01:12:16,719
Now they are afraid.

715
01:12:17,320 --> 01:12:19,439
They should be.

716
01:12:20,520 --> 01:12:24,559
They must also have heard
Nayman lost his head.

717
01:12:24,640 --> 01:12:27,159
Well, well..

718
01:12:30,080 --> 01:12:31,679
What about..

719
01:12:31,920 --> 01:12:34,439
..Lefke and Gemlik?

720
01:12:34,920 --> 01:12:37,799
They are digging pits on the roads to Gemlik.

721
01:12:38,240 --> 01:12:40,319
They're laying traps in the woods.

722
01:12:40,520 --> 01:12:43,399
But we know where they are.

723
01:12:44,680 --> 01:12:46,839
It's the same for Lefke, my Bey.

724
01:12:47,360 --> 01:12:49,199
They know the inevitable.

725
01:12:49,440 --> 01:12:52,639
Their lands will belong to Turks soon.

726
01:12:55,160 --> 01:12:57,159
Thank you.

727
01:12:58,360 --> 01:13:00,839
There is still time for these.

728
01:13:01,720 --> 01:13:05,119
It's time to speak of the bad.

729
01:13:07,960 --> 01:13:09,839
Lord Valens..

730
01:13:10,200 --> 01:13:12,999
...went to Constantinople in haste.

731
01:13:14,200 --> 01:13:17,999
He lost Nayman. He lost the commanders.

732
01:13:18,880 --> 01:13:22,399
He lost the troop that
he surely thought would kill us.

733
01:13:24,720 --> 01:13:26,839
He went to Constantinople...

734
01:13:27,560 --> 01:13:29,879
...to gain strength.

735
01:13:30,960 --> 01:13:33,119
If he succeeds..

736
01:13:34,040 --> 01:13:36,719
..comes back with an army

737
01:13:39,160 --> 01:13:41,239
..then..

738
01:13:42,440 --> 01:13:45,239
...we will have a tough battle.

739
01:14:01,640 --> 01:14:04,879
I'm ignoring the disrespect of your entrance.

740
01:14:05,760 --> 01:14:08,039
What do you want, Valens?

741
01:14:08,920 --> 01:14:12,759
That's exactly why I'm here, Emperor.

742
01:14:15,720 --> 01:14:18,719
Even your aide is whining like a kid.

743
01:14:22,840 --> 01:14:25,559
For God's sake

744
01:14:27,440 --> 01:14:29,679
...what does Byzantine have?

745
01:14:30,720 --> 01:14:32,839
Where is the Roman spirit?

746
01:14:33,280 --> 01:14:35,519
Where are the powerful men?

747
01:14:36,880 --> 01:14:39,439
Everyone hides like a woman...

748
01:14:40,440 --> 01:14:42,679
..and whines like a kid.

749
01:14:44,240 --> 01:14:45,599
I will...

750
01:14:46,440 --> 01:14:48,999
...save Byzantine from the Turks.

751
01:14:50,120 --> 01:14:54,119
Give the lordship to your whining politicians.

752
01:14:56,280 --> 01:14:58,319
I will take your army.

753
01:14:58,920 --> 01:15:00,879
And as before

754
01:15:01,080 --> 01:15:04,559
...I will lead the army as Commander Mouzalon.

755
01:15:05,680 --> 01:15:07,759
Tell me what happened.

756
01:15:08,760 --> 01:15:12,239
Osman killed Nayman.

757
01:15:12,600 --> 01:15:14,839
He destroyed my troops.

758
01:15:15,520 --> 01:15:19,879
And now he's preparing to march
to Koyunhisar and Lefke.

759
01:15:21,680 --> 01:15:24,479
I will destroy him in a pitched battle.

760
01:15:26,000 --> 01:15:28,839
Osman helped me a lot.

761
01:15:30,400 --> 01:15:33,439
But if he has set his eyes on our lands,

762
01:15:34,080 --> 01:15:36,479
...we will scratch his eyes out.

763
01:15:39,440 --> 01:15:44,799
You already asked for an army from your friends
in the west without asking me. Lord Valens.

764
01:15:45,480 --> 01:15:48,719
I'm not a Lord anymore.

765
01:15:49,840 --> 01:15:52,439
I'm the commander of Byzantine army.

766
01:15:55,160 --> 01:15:57,639
I will destroy Osman's dreams.

767
01:15:58,080 --> 01:15:59,679
By capturing Koyunhisar,

768
01:15:59,840 --> 01:16:03,039
...he's trying to disconnect Bursa from Iznik.

769
01:16:03,760 --> 01:16:07,639
Osman is besieging us more every passing day.

770
01:16:09,920 --> 01:16:11,359
Give your army..

771
01:16:11,520 --> 01:16:14,119
...under my command. Emperor.

772
01:16:16,800 --> 01:16:21,159
When I last gave the army to Prince Kantakouzenos,

773
01:16:21,800 --> 01:16:24,199
..he threatened my throne.

774
01:16:26,960 --> 01:16:30,159
How will I know you won't do the same?

775
01:16:31,160 --> 01:16:32,479
I am the man...

776
01:16:33,520 --> 01:16:35,559
...who got threatened by spears
on his neck!

777
01:16:35,800 --> 01:16:38,479
...for the glory of Byzantine.

778
01:16:38,960 --> 01:16:42,719
I am not a man who wants throne...

779
01:16:44,000 --> 01:16:46,199
..but a man who leaves a title for Byzantine.

780
01:16:47,880 --> 01:16:50,519
You must trust me, Emperor.

781
01:16:51,560 --> 01:16:55,599
If you didn't, it would be a huge mistake.

782
01:17:16,960 --> 01:17:18,919
Soldiers.

783
01:17:33,720 --> 01:17:36,799
You will have the army, Commander Mouzalon.

784
01:17:39,600 --> 01:17:42,759
If Osman attempts to destroy us,

785
01:17:43,360 --> 01:17:46,479
...you will respond to him the way he deserves.

786
01:17:49,840 --> 01:17:52,279
Mighty Emperor.

787
01:17:53,000 --> 01:17:54,799
I intend to..

788
01:17:55,160 --> 01:17:57,719
...destroy Osman in Bafeus Plains...

789
01:17:58,120 --> 01:18:00,759
...where is he advancing.

790
01:18:01,520 --> 01:18:03,119
For this reason

791
01:18:03,320 --> 01:18:07,519
...we need to prepare an army
consisted of the best soldiers.

792
01:18:11,840 --> 01:18:14,999
Leo, get prepared.

793
01:18:15,400 --> 01:18:18,719
Soldiers will met Commander Mouzalon.

794
01:18:30,400 --> 01:18:33,799
My Bey, if he gets the army

795
01:18:34,880 --> 01:18:36,719
..what will we do?

796
01:18:37,360 --> 01:18:39,999
Whatever army he recruits

797
01:18:41,520 --> 01:18:43,399
...we won't stop.

798
01:18:43,760 --> 01:18:45,199
As I said,

799
01:18:45,440 --> 01:18:49,079
..Lefke, Kestel and Gemlik.

800
01:18:50,240 --> 01:18:52,639
These will wait for now.

801
01:18:56,120 --> 01:18:58,879
But not Koyunhisar.

802
01:19:03,800 --> 01:19:06,119
We didn't send messages to villages in vain.

803
01:19:06,800 --> 01:19:09,239
We didn't send message to tribes in vain.

804
01:19:09,320 --> 01:19:12,799
With the troops to be recruited there,

805
01:19:13,000 --> 01:19:15,719
...we will be an one-body army.

806
01:19:16,160 --> 01:19:18,919
And we'll march to Koyunhisa

807
01:19:24,040 --> 01:19:25,559
My Bey.

808
01:19:26,080 --> 01:19:29,519
Do you have any information about the army...

809
01:19:29,640 --> 01:19:31,759
...which will come from Constantinople?

810
01:19:32,240 --> 01:19:35,279
We don't know how many
or how well they are equipped.

811
01:19:35,480 --> 01:19:37,799
We should know about the army first.

812
01:19:37,920 --> 01:19:39,719
So we'll know if we should..

813
01:19:39,840 --> 01:19:41,759
...hit and run or fight in a pitch.

814
01:19:41,960 --> 01:19:44,719
My Bey, is this the right time for a siege?

815
01:19:45,600 --> 01:19:47,919
Just be patient.

816
01:19:48,880 --> 01:19:50,599
Be patient.

817
01:19:52,720 --> 01:19:54,959
In Constantinople,

818
01:19:55,440 --> 01:19:58,399
...we have an intelligence service.

819
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:03,559
They told us that Lord Valens went there.

820
01:20:04,120 --> 01:20:05,719
Now they will tell us...

821
01:20:05,960 --> 01:20:08,879
...what he's going to do next.

822
01:20:09,560 --> 01:20:12,039
And by that time,

823
01:20:13,880 --> 01:20:16,239
...you'll have finished the preparations.

824
01:20:19,320 --> 01:20:20,759
My Bey

825
01:20:21,000 --> 01:20:23,199
...if we are caught during the siege,

826
01:20:23,520 --> 01:20:25,679
...they will destroy us.

827
01:20:26,880 --> 01:20:29,359
I said we would take Koyunhisar.

828
01:20:30,280 --> 01:20:31,959
I didn't say we'd besiege it.

829
01:20:34,160 --> 01:20:37,999
If we are to fight in the pitch,

830
01:20:38,920 --> 01:20:40,639
...we'll fight.

831
01:20:40,720 --> 01:20:43,439
If we are to lay an ambush,

832
01:20:43,520 --> 01:20:45,719
...we will lay an ambush.

833
01:20:46,520 --> 01:20:49,679
If we are to retreat

834
01:20:50,760 --> 01:20:53,039
..we will retreat.

835
01:20:55,360 --> 01:20:57,759
But I never conquer..

836
01:20:58,320 --> 01:21:00,479
...according to the moves of heathens.

837
01:21:00,960 --> 01:21:03,279
As my Bey orders.

838
01:21:03,760 --> 01:21:05,639
The council is over.

839
01:21:12,280 --> 01:21:14,159
Beys.

840
01:21:16,040 --> 01:21:18,079
Now listen to me carefully.

841
01:21:20,240 --> 01:21:22,279
The army that will come against us...

842
01:21:23,280 --> 01:21:25,519
..is the most difficult test..

843
01:21:25,880 --> 01:21:28,199
...we will ever experience.

844
01:21:29,080 --> 01:21:30,559
We will..

845
01:21:30,960 --> 01:21:32,719
...fight...

846
01:21:33,360 --> 01:21:35,959
...against the Byzantine army...

847
01:21:36,840 --> 01:21:39,519
...as the owners of this border alone.

848
01:21:40,520 --> 01:21:43,159
The thing that succeeds
in defeating the empire...

849
01:21:45,960 --> 01:21:48,319
..is the state now.

850
01:21:49,800 --> 01:21:52,239
Don't forget this.

851
01:21:59,120 --> 01:22:00,519
You can go.

852
01:22:24,840 --> 01:22:26,479
Do you know me?

853
01:22:27,760 --> 01:22:29,679
Commander Mouzalon.

854
01:22:31,400 --> 01:22:34,319
They always tell your stories at quarters.

855
01:22:37,480 --> 01:22:38,959
Good.

856
01:22:39,840 --> 01:22:42,119
Now a new legend will be written...

857
01:22:42,360 --> 01:22:44,559
...at my command.

858
01:22:49,040 --> 01:22:51,879
You will experience what you've heard.

859
01:22:53,320 --> 01:22:57,079
We will send Turks away from
these lands forever, Commander Mouzalon.

860
01:23:01,520 --> 01:23:03,799
Bad times come, soldier.

861
01:23:05,000 --> 01:23:07,199
Bad times..

862
01:23:07,400 --> 01:23:09,479
...bring strong men.

863
01:23:11,600 --> 01:23:15,239
Strong men fight.

864
01:23:17,040 --> 01:23:19,239
And they bring peaceful days.

865
01:23:19,720 --> 01:23:22,919
But... peaceful days...

866
01:23:24,320 --> 01:23:26,319
...bring weak men.

867
01:23:28,000 --> 01:23:30,279
Those weak and miserable men...

868
01:23:31,200 --> 01:23:33,239
...bring bad times again.

869
01:23:35,400 --> 01:23:37,359
We know who the weak men are.

870
01:23:38,000 --> 01:23:39,759
Then who are..

871
01:23:40,600 --> 01:23:43,639
..the ones who will bring
the Byzantium to its feet again?

872
01:23:43,800 --> 01:23:44,919
We are!

873
01:23:46,080 --> 01:23:47,519
We are.

874
01:23:49,720 --> 01:23:52,039
They made Byzantium kneel.

875
01:23:54,440 --> 01:23:57,239
And we will make it stronger than before.

876
01:24:00,840 --> 01:24:02,079
Commanders.

877
01:24:03,520 --> 01:24:06,759
May your swords be sharper than a lion's paw.

878
01:24:09,600 --> 01:24:12,319
You will leave the city without being seen.

879
01:24:12,680 --> 01:24:15,199
When you arrive in Osman's lands...

880
01:24:16,080 --> 01:24:18,679
..you will unite with the other army...

881
01:24:19,800 --> 01:24:22,319
...and turn into the furor of hell.

882
01:24:25,640 --> 01:24:28,119
We will fight for Byzantium!

883
01:24:28,800 --> 01:24:30,999
We were born for Byzantium..

884
01:24:31,720 --> 01:24:33,559
...and we can die for Byzantium.

885
01:24:35,600 --> 01:24:38,399
-For Byzantium.
-For Byzantium.

886
01:24:40,760 --> 01:24:42,919
I am going back to Bursa.

887
01:24:43,640 --> 01:24:46,599
You will bring death after me.

888
01:24:59,360 --> 01:25:02,759
May Allah salute you.

889
01:25:23,360 --> 01:25:25,599
O, Magnificent...

890
01:25:27,560 --> 01:25:30,079
...O, retributive justice!

891
01:25:31,840 --> 01:25:34,919
...O, my Allah, who resolves things.

892
01:25:36,080 --> 01:25:37,999
You made us responsible...

893
01:25:38,240 --> 01:25:39,759
..for the war..

894
01:25:41,160 --> 01:25:43,439
...for the battle.

895
01:25:44,560 --> 01:25:46,119
And we are trying hard to...

896
01:25:46,440 --> 01:25:50,319
...deserve being on Your way, my Allah.

897
01:25:54,120 --> 01:25:55,999
The victory...

898
01:25:57,080 --> 01:25:59,159
..and the defeat..

899
01:25:59,840 --> 01:26:01,559
...comes from You, my Allah.

900
01:26:04,520 --> 01:26:07,639
O, the Most Merciful..

901
01:26:09,080 --> 01:26:10,879
..O my Creator..

902
01:26:12,000 --> 01:26:14,519
Tomorrow, we will set out on a difficult road.

903
01:26:15,000 --> 01:26:17,759
Enlighten our way, my Allah.

904
01:26:18,600 --> 01:26:19,879
My Allah...

905
01:26:21,080 --> 01:26:26,159
...do not test us with an ending
which will make the cruel laugh, my Allah.

906
01:26:27,600 --> 01:26:29,079
My Allah..

907
01:26:29,680 --> 01:26:31,959
May You grant us a victory which will...

908
01:26:33,120 --> 01:26:37,759
...make the oppressed smile and
Muslims experience the joy of bairam.

909
01:26:39,640 --> 01:26:40,999
My Allah.

910
01:26:42,760 --> 01:26:45,039
For the sake of the the messenger of Allah
(PBUH) Nabi...

911
01:26:45,920 --> 01:26:49,039
...and the ones close to Allah..

912
01:26:50,520 --> 01:26:52,399
...allow us to enlighten the...

913
01:26:53,280 --> 01:26:57,679
...darkness of the infidels
with the light of Islam, O my Allah.

914
01:27:01,320 --> 01:27:02,559
My Allah...

915
01:27:04,760 --> 01:27:07,319
The valiants behind me..

916
01:27:08,640 --> 01:27:10,639
..are the soldiers of Islam's army.

917
01:27:11,760 --> 01:27:14,639
Grant us with the fate of Your ashabs...

918
01:27:15,360 --> 01:27:19,679
..who were victorious in Badr and Khaybar.

919
01:27:22,040 --> 01:27:23,559
Grant us..

920
01:27:24,320 --> 01:27:28,599
...so that we can be granted with
establishing a state that will...

921
01:27:29,160 --> 01:27:31,879
...place the sanjak of Islam all over the world.

922
01:27:34,400 --> 01:27:35,879
My Allah...

923
01:27:37,160 --> 01:27:39,479
Grant us with a...

924
01:27:40,840 --> 01:27:42,959
...glorious victory.

925
01:27:44,080 --> 01:27:46,239
Ameen, my Allah.

926
01:27:49,760 --> 01:27:51,279
Ameen, my Allah.

927
01:28:21,320 --> 01:28:22,639
Load it.

928
01:28:31,720 --> 01:28:33,079
May it be easy sisters.

929
01:28:33,240 --> 01:28:35,319
Thank you Malhun Hatun.

930
01:28:35,480 --> 01:28:37,399
Keep your eyes wide open.

931
01:28:37,520 --> 01:28:39,879
A mistake would cause someone to die.

932
01:28:42,800 --> 01:28:44,879
Thank you for your works Hatuns.

933
01:28:45,000 --> 01:28:47,639
Thank you Malhun Hatun.

934
01:28:47,760 --> 01:28:49,479
May our holy war be mubarak.

935
01:28:49,520 --> 01:28:51,919
If Allah permits, Malhun Hatun.

936
01:28:57,880 --> 01:28:59,759
Praise be!

937
01:29:00,440 --> 01:29:02,639
Look how she's working.

938
01:29:04,000 --> 01:29:05,639
She is my woman after all.

939
01:29:14,360 --> 01:29:16,279
You rascal!

940
01:29:16,440 --> 01:29:18,279
Why are you standing still?

941
01:29:18,920 --> 01:29:20,639
-Mother?
-Mother.

942
01:29:20,720 --> 01:29:22,759
Of course!

943
01:29:24,560 --> 01:29:26,999
Take water there and take it to Ulgen.

944
01:29:27,280 --> 01:29:28,599
Help her a bit.

945
01:29:28,960 --> 01:29:31,319
Instead of just looking, do some work!

946
01:29:31,600 --> 01:29:34,239
There's a battle ahead!

947
01:29:36,040 --> 01:29:38,999
Come on! Come on!

948
01:30:05,720 --> 01:30:08,959
-My Ulgen.
-Yes, my Cerkutay?

949
01:30:11,480 --> 01:30:14,319
-My Ulgen.
-Yes, my Cerkutay?

950
01:30:18,000 --> 01:30:19,119
Today,

951
01:30:20,680 --> 01:30:22,679
you look so beautiful.

952
01:30:23,760 --> 01:30:25,999
-Really?
-Really.

953
01:30:27,200 --> 01:30:28,719
You too

954
01:30:29,280 --> 01:30:31,719
you look like a soldier.

955
01:30:32,320 --> 01:30:34,839
You know, don't make me talk about it.

956
01:30:38,360 --> 01:30:40,239
Should I put some bulgur in it?

957
01:30:40,600 --> 01:30:42,359
All right, go get it.

958
01:30:52,920 --> 01:30:55,679
Go Cerkutay! Go now, go!

959
01:30:56,960 --> 01:31:00,239
You're doing work but you're
looking at Ulgen at the same time.

960
01:31:00,480 --> 01:31:02,599
-Come on, come on!
-Mother, but...

961
01:31:02,720 --> 01:31:04,399
Go away!

962
01:31:05,480 --> 01:31:07,559
Go and do some other work.

963
01:31:12,120 --> 01:31:15,639
All right but we just married.

964
01:31:16,960 --> 01:31:20,039
Ulgen, your mother won't let us be alone.

965
01:31:20,240 --> 01:31:22,599
All right, don't worry.

966
01:31:25,240 --> 01:31:28,199
May Allah make
your conversation last forever.

967
01:31:28,320 --> 01:31:29,599
Aameen.

968
01:31:31,320 --> 01:31:33,439
How can we do work with them?

969
01:31:33,760 --> 01:31:36,559
We say there's battle ahead.

970
01:31:37,040 --> 01:31:38,959
Do you trust your double sword?

971
01:31:39,560 --> 01:31:41,479
Try to get along.

972
01:31:41,880 --> 01:31:44,999
I trust your prayers, mother!

973
01:31:45,080 --> 01:31:46,759
Angel mother.

974
01:31:46,880 --> 01:31:50,319
But I guess you're tired,
that's why you're so grumpy.

975
01:31:50,960 --> 01:31:52,639
Have a seat, if you want.

976
01:31:52,880 --> 01:31:55,119
You're old after all.

977
01:31:58,280 --> 01:32:00,399
-What am I?
-Mother!

978
01:32:00,440 --> 01:32:02,599
He said you're too tired, mother.

979
01:32:03,920 --> 01:32:05,639
Right, Malhun Hatun?

980
01:32:05,720 --> 01:32:08,919
Now, since we will be behind Osman Bey,

981
01:32:09,040 --> 01:32:12,639
they are coming from all over,
O praise be!

982
01:32:13,240 --> 01:32:15,399
We need to cook lots of food.

983
01:32:19,760 --> 01:32:21,519
Praise be!

984
01:32:21,720 --> 01:32:25,479
We will make it on time for sure!

985
01:32:26,120 --> 01:32:27,879
Praise be!

986
01:32:30,120 --> 01:32:33,519
Our blood is boiling
just like the food in this cauldron.

987
01:32:34,280 --> 01:32:35,719
Be quiet.

988
01:32:37,040 --> 01:32:41,159
It will be ready on time, the food will be
ready just like all those soldiers.

989
01:32:42,360 --> 01:32:43,519
Anyway.

990
01:32:44,320 --> 01:32:45,759
I should get going.

991
01:32:46,280 --> 01:32:49,879
I took this duty just to see you.

992
01:32:51,920 --> 01:32:53,759
Know my value.

993
01:32:57,440 --> 01:32:59,239
Come on, leave!

994
01:33:00,080 --> 01:33:02,559
You need battlefield.

995
01:33:04,760 --> 01:33:07,559
May your sword not be wasted.

996
01:33:09,080 --> 01:33:10,599
May Allah help you.

997
01:33:10,920 --> 01:33:12,559
My brave son.

998
01:33:23,400 --> 01:33:24,719
Mother..

999
01:33:25,240 --> 01:33:27,799
I can't hold it anymore let me kiss your hand.

1000
01:33:33,080 --> 01:33:34,759
May you be safe on the road.

1001
01:33:36,240 --> 01:33:38,399
May Allah help you.

1002
01:33:43,080 --> 01:33:44,959
Go now.

1003
01:33:56,360 --> 01:33:57,959
Let us go, alps!

1004
01:35:01,640 --> 01:35:05,399
Osman Bey, Lord Valens and
Emperor Andronikos have made an alliance.

1005
01:35:06,000 --> 01:35:08,359
A huge army of barbarians is present.

1006
01:35:09,040 --> 01:35:11,119
This army serves a single purpose.

1007
01:35:11,280 --> 01:35:14,879
They won't stop until they banish you
and muslims from this land.

1008
01:35:20,040 --> 01:35:22,359
It doesn't matter how many you come.

1009
01:35:23,720 --> 01:35:26,399
Gather all armies if you'd like.

1010
01:36:22,600 --> 01:36:24,159
Iltutan.

1011
01:36:26,120 --> 01:36:27,679
Who are these people?

1012
01:36:44,720 --> 01:36:47,159
Let us find out.

1013
01:36:47,920 --> 01:36:49,479
But for that..

1014
01:36:50,920 --> 01:36:53,359
We need to appear with plain clothes.

1015
01:37:56,680 --> 01:37:58,039
Peace be upon you.

1016
01:37:59,040 --> 01:38:00,959
Peace be upon you too.

1017
01:38:19,760 --> 01:38:22,759
-Where are you going?
-We will visit Yenisehir.

1018
01:38:25,680 --> 01:38:29,079
-What are you going to do in Yenisehir?
-What do you think? We were invited to the war.

1019
01:38:29,760 --> 01:38:32,439
Osman Bey called for Beys from everywhere.

1020
01:38:40,160 --> 01:38:41,199
However..

1021
01:38:42,800 --> 01:38:45,439
You seem tired.

1022
01:38:51,360 --> 01:38:53,279
Why do you even bother?

1023
01:38:53,480 --> 01:38:55,519
We are tired, but not coward.

1024
01:38:57,360 --> 01:38:59,479
Alright, alright.

1025
01:39:01,400 --> 01:39:04,439
Now you go to Yenisehir
as Osman Bey called you.

1026
01:39:05,760 --> 01:39:07,919
I did not ask the important question.

1027
01:39:10,440 --> 01:39:11,799
Where do you come from?

1028
01:39:12,240 --> 01:39:14,639
We have been riding from Kipcak.

1029
01:39:14,840 --> 01:39:17,279
Many of our steed have fallen on the way.

1030
01:39:17,680 --> 01:39:19,279
These are what's left.

1031
01:39:29,800 --> 01:39:31,599
Kipcak Lands you say?

1032
01:39:38,960 --> 01:39:41,399
Kipcak Lands are pretty far away.

1033
01:39:42,840 --> 01:39:45,359
-For how many days have you been on road?
-Fifteen.

1034
01:39:53,160 --> 01:39:55,679
The calling of Osman Bey..

1035
01:39:56,600 --> 01:39:58,359
...is quite recent.

1036
01:39:58,520 --> 01:39:59,959
We heard him on the way.

1037
01:40:00,400 --> 01:40:02,559
We come, without being called to.

1038
01:40:02,720 --> 01:40:04,519
War is always present.

1039
01:40:04,800 --> 01:40:07,759
You know the calling,
then why are you sitting here?

1040
01:40:07,880 --> 01:40:10,919
Are you running away from the battle?

1041
01:40:12,800 --> 01:40:14,319
What do you know?

1042
01:40:14,960 --> 01:40:17,279
Maybe I will face them alone?

1043
01:40:17,800 --> 01:40:20,199
And I am sitting here before that.

1044
01:40:25,440 --> 01:40:28,639
Whatever, don't let me hold you.

1045
01:40:29,160 --> 01:40:31,079
Be on your way to Yenisehir.

1046
01:40:31,360 --> 01:40:33,079
We will surely meet there.

1047
01:40:33,200 --> 01:40:35,599
-If Allah permits.
-Safe travels.

1048
01:40:36,920 --> 01:40:38,759
Thank you, you too.

1049
01:40:40,200 --> 01:40:42,519
-Goodbye.
-Quickly, we're leaving.

1050
01:41:12,560 --> 01:41:13,999
Kipcak Lands..

1051
01:41:15,360 --> 01:41:17,279
Oi Praise be!

1052
01:41:19,440 --> 01:41:23,479
As long as there are valiants
whose hearts are rooted in this land..

1053
01:41:24,120 --> 01:41:26,519
We are in good hands.

1054
01:41:28,400 --> 01:41:30,799
They will all be destroyed.

1055
01:41:40,680 --> 01:41:43,399
When do you think the battle will begin, brother?

1056
01:41:44,600 --> 01:41:48,119
We will be informed, brother.
Osman Bey will inform everyone.

1057
01:41:57,880 --> 01:42:00,679
In the name of Allah!
Allah is eternal!

1058
01:42:00,840 --> 01:42:02,439
Allah is right!

1059
01:42:02,640 --> 01:42:06,599
Allah is eternal!

1060
01:42:07,120 --> 01:42:08,929
-Allah is right!
- Allah is eternal!

1061
01:42:08,964 --> 01:42:10,774
How is it going, valiants?

1062
01:42:11,120 --> 01:42:13,519
-Thank you, Kumral Abdal.
-Thank you.

1063
01:42:13,920 --> 01:42:15,279
Praise be!

1064
01:42:16,240 --> 01:42:18,839
Just like how your ancestors melted iron..

1065
01:42:19,840 --> 01:42:22,279
You are grasping it just as strong.

1066
01:42:23,080 --> 01:42:25,439
How did they melt it Kumral Abdal?

1067
01:42:25,760 --> 01:42:27,519
Tell us, will you?

1068
01:42:34,680 --> 01:42:36,999
A mountain of iron.

1069
01:42:37,920 --> 01:42:41,079
Turks want to get out of Ergenekon Plains.

1070
01:42:42,800 --> 01:42:44,799
However, everywhere is closed.

1071
01:42:45,240 --> 01:42:47,159
They try to find a way.

1072
01:42:47,680 --> 01:42:49,479
When they can't find a way..

1073
01:42:49,960 --> 01:42:52,479
Their only solution is making way.

1074
01:42:53,800 --> 01:42:55,479
To make way..

1075
01:42:55,960 --> 01:42:58,879
They start melting the iron mountain.

1076
01:42:59,000 --> 01:43:02,479
They lay a line of wood

1077
01:43:02,720 --> 01:43:04,959
And a line of coal, in front of the
iron mountain.

1078
01:43:05,280 --> 01:43:09,079
They put seventy different fires
to seventy different spots.

1079
01:43:12,960 --> 01:43:15,399
The fires raise at the same time.

1080
01:43:17,120 --> 01:43:19,919
Iron melts, and makes way.

1081
01:43:21,400 --> 01:43:23,279
They find their way.

1082
01:43:24,840 --> 01:43:26,439
With unity.

1083
01:43:30,240 --> 01:43:32,959
Now, we have such a mountain in front of us.

1084
01:43:34,480 --> 01:43:35,959
It may not be iron..

1085
01:43:36,360 --> 01:43:39,559
But enemies and traitors confront us.

1086
01:43:41,320 --> 01:43:45,159
So we will be one under Osman Bey,
to make path.

1087
01:43:45,600 --> 01:43:49,399
We make swords out of the..

1088
01:43:49,920 --> 01:43:51,879
...Iron we melted before.

1089
01:43:52,800 --> 01:43:54,439
We will make way.

1090
01:43:54,800 --> 01:43:59,639
Our children and their children
will walk on this path.

1091
01:44:02,440 --> 01:44:04,239
We will be one.

1092
01:44:04,960 --> 01:44:07,239
We will unite.

1093
01:44:18,680 --> 01:44:22,079
- Allah is eternal.
- Allah is right!

1094
01:44:22,440 --> 01:44:23,879
Allah is eternal!

1095
01:44:24,080 --> 01:44:25,799
Praise be!

1096
01:44:26,280 --> 01:44:29,639
Now it is time to put
these swords in enemies' chests.

1097
01:44:30,680 --> 01:44:33,039
- Allah is eternal.
- Allah is right!

1098
01:44:33,120 --> 01:44:37,259
- Allah is eternal.
- Allah is right!

1099
01:45:05,000 --> 01:45:06,639
Gokcekiz, quickly.

1100
01:45:12,800 --> 01:45:15,319
My sisters, now.

1101
01:45:17,280 --> 01:45:19,639
O Allah!

1102
01:45:25,920 --> 01:45:27,439
Now.

1103
01:45:28,040 --> 01:45:30,439
O Allah!

1104
01:45:40,600 --> 01:45:44,159
You have to take a step and
take it out using your shoulder.

1105
01:45:44,320 --> 01:45:47,359
Use your shoulders with a step.

1106
01:45:48,040 --> 01:45:49,679
Now.

1107
01:45:57,320 --> 01:45:58,599
Now!

1108
01:45:59,320 --> 01:46:01,399
Ya Haqq!

1109
01:46:04,960 --> 01:46:07,639
Praise be, praise be!

1110
01:46:09,200 --> 01:46:10,959
Wait for a while.

1111
01:46:18,600 --> 01:46:19,719
Ready.

1112
01:46:22,640 --> 01:46:23,639
Shoot!

1113
01:46:27,360 --> 01:46:28,599
Draw!

1114
01:46:30,240 --> 01:46:31,479
Shoot!

1115
01:46:34,480 --> 01:46:35,479
Get up!

1116
01:46:37,000 --> 01:46:38,239
Ready.

1117
01:46:38,960 --> 01:46:40,639
Shoot!

1118
01:46:46,920 --> 01:46:48,879
If you hold so tight

1119
01:46:49,360 --> 01:46:52,239
you will wound your own hand before the enemy.

1120
01:46:54,520 --> 01:46:56,199
Hold it softly.

1121
01:47:00,640 --> 01:47:02,719
Come on, praise be!

1122
01:47:03,680 --> 01:47:05,159
Wait.

1123
01:47:16,080 --> 01:47:19,319
The ones who came from
the tribes are being trained my Bala.

1124
01:47:19,720 --> 01:47:21,919
Praise be, praise be.

1125
01:47:28,120 --> 01:47:29,799
Keep going!

1126
01:47:32,800 --> 01:47:36,559
In our tribes, in our cities
whichever stone we lift,

1127
01:47:36,880 --> 01:47:39,799
we find hearts that is
yearning for holy war.

1128
01:47:39,880 --> 01:47:41,199
That's right.

1129
01:47:44,400 --> 01:47:47,039
I wouldn't expect to see
this much as well, Bala.

1130
01:47:47,680 --> 01:47:49,359
But we grew bigger.

1131
01:47:51,120 --> 01:47:53,879
Our case also grew bigger and spread.

1132
01:47:55,200 --> 01:47:56,959
Thank Allah.

1133
01:47:57,760 --> 01:47:59,639
It will spread wider, if Allah permits.

1134
01:48:00,560 --> 01:48:03,439
It will spread to the walls,
beyond the seas.

1135
01:48:04,960 --> 01:48:07,559
Let us be glorious in this battle as well.

1136
01:48:07,720 --> 01:48:09,439
I hope so.

1137
01:48:10,280 --> 01:48:12,039
I hope so.

1138
01:48:13,560 --> 01:48:16,199
Hold it tighter, tighter.

1139
01:48:17,480 --> 01:48:19,039
Praise be.

1140
01:48:20,720 --> 01:48:22,239
Bala Hatun.

1141
01:48:23,320 --> 01:48:25,599
Train with me as well.

1142
01:48:28,040 --> 01:48:31,559
Esrigun Hatun, gladly.

1143
01:48:33,000 --> 01:48:34,399
Here.

1144
01:48:51,600 --> 01:48:52,759
Come on.

1145
01:49:52,600 --> 01:49:53,839
Praise be.

1146
01:49:54,760 --> 01:49:56,279
I wasn't expecting it.

1147
01:49:56,640 --> 01:49:59,199
You are good at sword battle, Bala Hatun.

1148
01:50:01,560 --> 01:50:02,919
Thank you.

1149
01:50:03,400 --> 01:50:05,319
You are also pretty tough.

1150
01:50:06,320 --> 01:50:07,599
Thank you.

1151
01:50:12,320 --> 01:50:14,239
It is time!

1152
01:50:22,280 --> 01:50:24,959
Brave women of The Sisters!

1153
01:50:25,360 --> 01:50:28,679
May my Creator reward you all for your hard work.

1154
01:50:29,040 --> 01:50:30,159
Aameen.

1155
01:50:30,400 --> 01:50:32,719
I can see that you're getting impatient.

1156
01:50:32,960 --> 01:50:34,759
Don't think that I can't see it.

1157
01:50:34,960 --> 01:50:37,359
But the patience ends up with soundness.

1158
01:50:37,880 --> 01:50:41,599
Even the name of the infidels
will be removed from these lands.

1159
01:50:41,880 --> 01:50:45,199
We will plant the banner
of Islam on all of the towers.

1160
01:50:47,720 --> 01:50:51,519
Allah is the greatest!

1161
01:50:51,680 --> 01:50:57,079
Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest!

1162
01:50:58,160 --> 01:50:59,359
Praise be!

1163
01:51:00,320 --> 01:51:04,239
Come on, it is time to renew our vow.

1164
01:51:05,160 --> 01:51:07,439
Bring the henna Gokee.

1165
01:51:13,360 --> 01:51:15,359
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate.

1166
01:51:19,080 --> 01:51:23,319
A warrior's essence resides in sword,
As sacrifice's essence abides in blood.

1167
01:51:23,360 --> 01:51:27,479
Soldiers face with a sister's dare,
In martyrdom, they're made aware.

1168
01:51:28,600 --> 01:51:32,479
Martyrdom, our breath's embrace,
War courses through our veins with grace.

1169
01:51:32,480 --> 01:51:36,959
If sherbet's thirst consumes your desire,
Deceive your heart with martyrdom's fire.

1170
01:51:37,040 --> 01:51:38,759
The Sisters, The Sisters!

1171
01:51:39,000 --> 01:51:41,279
they bear Fatma Ana's guiding hand

1172
01:51:41,560 --> 01:51:44,639
A sister challenges men
in martyrdom's grand.

1173
01:51:49,680 --> 01:51:51,399
May Allah bless you.

1174
01:51:56,400 --> 01:51:58,519
Before I came to the Frontiers

1175
01:51:58,920 --> 01:52:01,639
I was curious about you Sisters the most.

1176
01:52:02,280 --> 01:52:03,639
Then

1177
01:52:03,880 --> 01:52:07,479
are you ready to fight side by side
with The Sisters, Esrigun Hatun?

1178
01:52:09,200 --> 01:52:11,799
I'm ready of course, Bala Hatun.

1179
01:52:12,600 --> 01:52:14,479
No, you're not.

1180
01:52:18,040 --> 01:52:19,559
Come here.

1181
01:52:21,080 --> 01:52:23,159
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate.

1182
01:52:25,720 --> 01:52:27,759
You're ready now.

1183
01:52:28,520 --> 01:52:31,919
We took an oath,
we do not fight without henna.

1184
01:52:34,560 --> 01:52:38,159
Then, since the hennas are ready,

1185
01:52:38,400 --> 01:52:40,319
we can set out.

1186
01:52:40,600 --> 01:52:42,679
Come on Sisters, to the horses.

1187
01:52:42,880 --> 01:52:45,679
The battle awaits us, come on.

1188
01:53:10,320 --> 01:53:12,999
My Bey. You brought good news, I hope.

1189
01:53:13,520 --> 01:53:15,399
The news is not good.

1190
01:53:16,560 --> 01:53:18,999
But we encountered the good on the way.

1191
01:53:22,720 --> 01:53:24,239
Lord Valens..

1192
01:53:25,200 --> 01:53:28,239
...made an agreement with Emperor Andronikos.

1193
01:53:30,640 --> 01:53:32,799
My Bey, why did they make an agreement?

1194
01:53:32,880 --> 01:53:35,599
According to the intelligence I've received...

1195
01:53:35,920 --> 01:53:39,199
...they built an army by
gathering the most savage soldiers...

1196
01:53:39,280 --> 01:53:40,999
...and they are coming on us.

1197
01:53:44,960 --> 01:53:47,799
They will be here within the shortest time.

1198
01:53:49,080 --> 01:53:51,959
What about the soldiers he called from the west?

1199
01:53:52,360 --> 01:53:53,919
Two armies want to unite.

1200
01:53:55,200 --> 01:53:57,199
But we will not let that happen.

1201
01:53:59,280 --> 01:54:02,159
They are coming at us all together, huh, my Bey?

1202
01:54:03,400 --> 01:54:04,919
What are we going to do, my Bey?

1203
01:54:05,320 --> 01:54:07,119
We will do the same thing..

1204
01:54:07,640 --> 01:54:09,999
...we always did. Bayindir.

1205
01:54:11,200 --> 01:54:13,199
We did not stop, and we won't stop.

1206
01:54:13,640 --> 01:54:15,279
Conquests will continue.

1207
01:54:18,080 --> 01:54:19,759
We will take Koyunhisa

1208
01:54:23,960 --> 01:54:26,799
My Bey. We didn't know how powerful they were.

1209
01:54:27,080 --> 01:54:30,559
Are we going to fight now although
we know how powerful they are?

1210
01:54:30,720 --> 01:54:31,919
Not us.

1211
01:54:33,240 --> 01:54:35,679
You will fight, Uraz Bey.

1212
01:54:40,640 --> 01:54:43,359
With Demirhan and Ozmen Bey.

1213
01:54:48,320 --> 01:54:50,679
Why did we build those catapults?

1214
01:54:51,080 --> 01:54:53,039
Why did we send news to the villages?

1215
01:54:53,560 --> 01:54:56,719
Now... With the Alps
who will come from the tribes...

1216
01:54:57,880 --> 01:54:59,879
...you will take Koyunhisar.

1217
01:55:00,280 --> 01:55:02,239
Yes my Bey.

1218
01:55:02,800 --> 01:55:05,319
What if they get attacked at that time, my Bey?

1219
01:55:05,560 --> 01:55:09,559
No. We will attack the army
which will come from the west.

1220
01:55:10,520 --> 01:55:13,519
We will never let those two armies unite.

1221
01:55:17,120 --> 01:55:19,839
Come on Beys. What are you waiting for?

1222
01:55:21,600 --> 01:55:23,839
Yes my Bey.

1223
01:55:29,760 --> 01:55:34,159
My Bey. One army comes from the Constantine
the other comes from the west, right?

1224
01:55:35,400 --> 01:55:36,679
Yes.

1225
01:55:36,960 --> 01:55:40,079
If we cannot defeat the army
which will come from the west...

1226
01:55:40,240 --> 01:55:42,439
...then we cannot defeat Valens' army.

1227
01:55:46,200 --> 01:55:48,479
We will split them in two...

1228
01:55:49,040 --> 01:55:51,319
...and destroy them.

1229
01:55:53,240 --> 01:55:54,479
My Bey.

1230
01:55:55,280 --> 01:55:58,159
Do we know something
about the army in the west?

1231
01:55:59,800 --> 01:56:02,079
Cerkutay...

1232
01:56:03,120 --> 01:56:04,519
Do we? Tell me.

1233
01:56:06,240 --> 01:56:09,399
We even know the number
of breaths they take, my Bey.

1234
01:56:12,160 --> 01:56:13,999
Good.

1235
01:56:23,400 --> 01:56:24,359
My Bey.

1236
01:56:25,680 --> 01:56:28,279
This dog has something to tell you.

1237
01:56:28,840 --> 01:56:30,919
We will kill you Turks!

1238
01:56:34,040 --> 01:56:35,519
You shouldn't have..

1239
01:56:43,120 --> 01:56:45,079
Now..

1240
01:56:48,120 --> 01:56:50,159
You will choose one of them.

1241
01:56:52,080 --> 01:56:53,319
You will..

1242
01:56:54,240 --> 01:56:57,679
...tell me everything you know about the army..

1243
01:56:58,160 --> 01:57:00,159
...you will tell me, so...

1244
01:57:01,120 --> 01:57:03,279
...I can set you free with ransom money.

1245
01:57:11,080 --> 01:57:13,479
No, stand up. Come.

1246
01:57:14,040 --> 01:57:17,239
Come on now... We just started.

1247
01:57:18,160 --> 01:57:20,159
You will tell me.

1248
01:57:21,560 --> 01:57:24,599
Stand up, stand up.

1249
01:57:25,080 --> 01:57:27,999
Stand up, stand up.

1250
01:57:28,720 --> 01:57:30,119
Or...

1251
01:57:31,200 --> 01:57:33,999
I will beat you to death.

1252
01:57:44,800 --> 01:57:47,119
Alright! Alright! I will tell you.

1253
01:57:53,360 --> 01:57:54,399
Balaban.

1254
01:57:57,920 --> 01:57:59,959
Now go to Yenisehir.

1255
01:58:00,360 --> 01:58:02,759
Go to the villages and places around...

1256
01:58:03,200 --> 01:58:05,879
...and bring the Alps who gathered for us.

1257
01:58:06,400 --> 01:58:08,399
Now that there is a war.

1258
01:58:08,840 --> 01:58:10,039
...let them all come!

1259
01:58:10,360 --> 01:58:13,119
-Yes my Bey.
-Thank you, thank you.

1260
01:58:14,640 --> 01:58:17,279
Alps! Beys.

1261
01:58:18,200 --> 01:58:19,879
We will destroy that army...

1262
01:58:21,480 --> 01:58:23,799
..before mid-afternoon.

1263
01:58:29,000 --> 01:58:31,039
Now listen to me carefully.

1264
01:58:37,000 --> 01:58:40,119
The wolf smells its prey.

1265
01:58:41,280 --> 01:58:44,039
But it waits for the right time to attack.

1266
01:58:45,840 --> 01:58:48,479
But it also makes its move to get it.

1267
01:58:50,200 --> 01:58:52,719
We will do the same. Here..

1268
01:58:53,680 --> 01:58:55,999
...the army of infidels that we will destroy...

1269
01:58:56,560 --> 01:59:00,079
...wants to come to our lands
by passing through Karayurt.

1270
01:59:00,960 --> 01:59:03,119
We'll turn the way
into hell for them.

1271
01:59:03,400 --> 01:59:07,039
The army will have rest near Kirmagara.

1272
01:59:07,320 --> 01:59:10,119
And our mission will start there.

1273
01:59:11,760 --> 01:59:14,079
We'll take their
strength first...

1274
01:59:14,360 --> 01:59:16,719
..and then their lives.

1275
01:59:21,920 --> 01:59:24,399
You'll release their horses.

1276
01:59:25,080 --> 01:59:27,799
And the army will have to advance on foot.

1277
01:59:51,280 --> 01:59:52,559
They will...

1278
01:59:52,560 --> 01:59:56,199
...bring the shields from behind
not to lose their speed.

1279
01:59:56,400 --> 01:59:59,079
Baysungur, Shamil.

1280
01:59:59,320 --> 02:00:00,799
Aykut.

1281
02:00:01,000 --> 02:00:03,559
You will first slow down
the carriage first...

1282
02:00:03,720 --> 02:00:05,719
..and then abduct it.

1283
02:00:37,600 --> 02:00:39,959
When we take the shields from them.

1284
02:00:40,240 --> 02:00:42,359
...they will remain defenseless.

1285
02:00:42,720 --> 02:00:44,479
But..

1286
02:00:44,920 --> 02:00:48,079
It won't be enough to shoot them with arrows only.

1287
02:00:48,280 --> 02:00:51,319
We'll unite with the soldiers coming from Yenisehir...

1288
02:00:51,680 --> 02:00:53,679
..and eradicate them.

1289
02:01:44,560 --> 02:01:46,519
This sword..

1290
02:01:46,960 --> 02:01:49,079
..will stick into your heart.

1291
02:01:54,520 --> 02:01:56,439
Commander Mouzalon.

1292
02:01:56,840 --> 02:01:59,039
-Leo.
-Sir.

1293
02:01:59,160 --> 02:02:02,399
Byzantines ships have been
detected off Yalakova coast.

1294
02:02:03,800 --> 02:02:05,839
Your army is coming, sir.

1295
02:02:07,640 --> 02:02:09,479
Let's go welcome them.

1296
02:02:11,240 --> 02:02:13,119
What about the other troops?

1297
02:02:13,880 --> 02:02:17,119
No news yet, but they are coming.

1298
02:02:23,560 --> 02:02:26,199
If something goes wrong,

1299
02:02:29,080 --> 02:02:31,759
...you will be the first to die, Leo.

1300
02:02:34,080 --> 02:02:36,759
The two armies will unite.

1301
02:02:37,520 --> 02:02:41,519
That's only how we can take Byzantine back.

1302
02:02:42,640 --> 02:02:44,879
Yes, sir.

1303
02:02:46,080 --> 02:02:47,559
Let's go.

1304
02:02:58,480 --> 02:03:00,359
Come on, come on.

1305
02:03:00,640 --> 02:03:03,719
-Hurry up!
-Bring it here.

1306
02:03:14,760 --> 02:03:16,839
Sacks here. Sacks here!

1307
02:03:17,280 --> 02:03:19,079
Yes, sir.

1308
02:03:19,720 --> 02:03:21,959
-Come on!
-Be careful.

1309
02:03:23,920 --> 02:03:25,599
Bring it.

1310
02:03:26,960 --> 02:03:29,479
Come on! Take it on your back!

1311
02:03:41,480 --> 02:03:43,679
Get your troops in order.

1312
02:03:44,080 --> 02:03:47,039
Encourage your soldiers with blood and bounty.

1313
02:03:48,240 --> 02:03:50,559
Place soldiers around.

1314
02:03:51,240 --> 02:03:53,959
Osman shouldn't know about our existence.

1315
02:03:54,400 --> 02:03:57,959
Finish all the preparations before
Commander Mouzalon arrives.

1316
02:03:57,960 --> 02:03:59,919
Yes, sir.

1317
02:04:04,040 --> 02:04:06,079
Move, move!

1318
02:04:41,480 --> 02:04:43,559
Come.

1319
02:04:46,480 --> 02:04:48,919
You're coming to your end.

1320
02:04:59,000 --> 02:05:00,159
My Bey.

1321
02:05:00,240 --> 02:05:01,799
Horses got released.

1322
02:05:01,880 --> 02:05:03,479
Baysungur sent a message too.

1323
02:05:03,560 --> 02:05:05,799
They captured the carriage.

1324
02:05:05,800 --> 02:05:07,839
Okay.

1325
02:05:08,440 --> 02:05:10,439
Okay.

1326
02:05:11,880 --> 02:05:14,439
Now it's our turn.

1327
02:05:14,560 --> 02:05:16,679
Alps.

1328
02:05:17,280 --> 02:05:19,319
Prepare the arrows.

1329
02:05:26,920 --> 02:05:29,599
Shoot the Turk's arrows!

1330
02:05:30,000 --> 02:05:31,319
Now.

1331
02:05:31,560 --> 02:05:33,799
-Ya Haqq!
-Ya Haqq!

1332
02:05:37,320 --> 02:05:40,679
Ya Haqq!

1333
02:05:50,640 --> 02:05:52,839
Now it's time to fight!

1334
02:05:55,480 --> 02:05:57,559
Come on, sisters!

1335
02:05:58,880 --> 02:06:00,319
Allah is the greatest!

1336
02:06:00,320 --> 02:06:02,519
-Come on!
-Allah is the greatest!

1337
02:06:58,040 --> 02:07:00,519
-Are you alright, my Bey?
-Come on.

1338
02:07:00,720 --> 02:07:02,519
Fight, come on!

1339
02:07:06,040 --> 02:07:09,399
Whoever sets his eyes on
my land will find his grave there!

1340
02:07:09,400 --> 02:07:10,839
Come on, soldiers!

1341
02:07:11,000 --> 02:07:14,559
Allah is the greatest!

1342
02:07:30,440 --> 02:07:32,439
-They're running off.
-Go!

1343
02:07:32,520 --> 02:07:35,199
-Alright.
-Cerkutay!

1344
02:07:38,640 --> 02:07:39,999
Come on!

1345
02:08:13,160 --> 02:08:15,559
My Bey, why didn't you say
you are Osman Bey?

1346
02:08:18,320 --> 02:08:20,279
So what?

1347
02:08:20,320 --> 02:08:22,959
-There is no Bey during a fight.
-You're right, my Bey.

1348
02:08:23,000 --> 02:08:24,359
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

1349
02:08:24,360 --> 02:08:25,879
-Live long.
-You too, my Bey.

1350
02:08:25,880 --> 02:08:27,279
Live long.

1351
02:08:27,320 --> 02:08:29,879
Now it's our turn to move.

1352
02:08:30,000 --> 02:08:31,599
You're right, my Bey.

1353
02:08:34,800 --> 02:08:36,679
Hurry up, come on!

1354
02:08:40,880 --> 02:08:43,159
Bring it over here.

1355
02:08:45,960 --> 02:08:47,959
-Get in line!
-Yes, sir.

1356
02:08:48,440 --> 02:08:49,959
Of course, sir!

1357
02:08:56,480 --> 02:08:58,759
Slow down! Careful!

1358
02:09:05,960 --> 02:09:08,599
Commander Mouzalon is coming!

1359
02:09:24,560 --> 02:09:26,599
Commander Mouzalon?

1360
02:09:27,120 --> 02:09:29,319
Commander Silvanus!

1361
02:09:31,080 --> 02:09:34,039
You took a great army with you...

1362
02:09:34,360 --> 02:09:37,159
...that was created to destroy Muslims.

1363
02:09:42,560 --> 02:09:44,479
Every one of our soldiers...

1364
02:09:44,640 --> 02:09:47,639
...will sharpen their swords with Muslim blood, sir.

1365
02:09:50,920 --> 02:09:52,679
Very soon.

1366
02:09:52,880 --> 02:09:54,959
...I will give them what they want.

1367
02:09:55,800 --> 02:09:58,319
The army my friends in the west sent...

1368
02:09:58,480 --> 02:10:00,199
..will be here soon.

1369
02:10:00,480 --> 02:10:04,359
And then the apocalypse of Turks will begin.

1370
02:10:05,800 --> 02:10:09,599
Osman must be celebrating his victory against Nayman,

1371
02:10:10,040 --> 02:10:13,239
...without being aware of the apocalypse approaching.

1372
02:10:13,320 --> 02:10:16,399
I'm looking forward to seeing the fear in Osman's face...

1373
02:10:16,440 --> 02:10:19,839
...when I attack him with my armies.

1374
02:10:20,320 --> 02:10:23,279
When Turks see our armies,

1375
02:10:23,280 --> 02:10:26,399
...they'll run back to the barren lands where they came from.

1376
02:10:26,440 --> 02:10:28,879
For years, they have ravished our lands.

1377
02:10:29,760 --> 02:10:32,439
We will show no mercy to them.

1378
02:10:33,720 --> 02:10:37,079
We will drive them off from these lands for eternity.

1379
02:10:38,320 --> 02:10:42,039
Today, I will bury Turks in the Bafeus Plains.

1380
02:10:47,600 --> 02:10:48,359
Bey.

1381
02:10:49,240 --> 02:10:51,079
We hit one of the armies.

1382
02:10:51,440 --> 02:10:53,959
We don't know the location of the other.

1383
02:10:54,080 --> 02:10:55,879
Beys first surround Koyunhisar.

1384
02:10:58,760 --> 02:11:00,959
What are we waiting for here?

1385
02:11:01,760 --> 02:11:03,719
Forgive me but..

1386
02:11:04,040 --> 02:11:05,959
Shall we go join them?

1387
02:11:06,080 --> 02:11:09,559
No, the most skilled hunter..

1388
02:11:10,720 --> 02:11:12,719
Is the patient one.

1389
02:11:14,160 --> 02:11:17,439
Didn't you spend days for one hunt?

1390
02:11:17,720 --> 02:11:19,799
I did, Bey, however..

1391
02:11:20,280 --> 02:11:24,039
-The animal was in front of us.
-Now it is in front of us as well.

1392
02:11:25,560 --> 02:11:27,559
Now we shot them.

1393
02:11:27,920 --> 02:11:29,839
We interfered their merging.

1394
02:11:30,360 --> 02:11:34,359
Now it is time to hit the army
that Valens brought from Constantinople.

1395
02:11:37,600 --> 02:11:40,679
The wounded we let go of will bring us to them.

1396
02:11:40,840 --> 02:11:42,519
We will hit them there.

1397
02:11:43,920 --> 02:11:45,919
If arrows won't be enough..

1398
02:11:46,360 --> 02:11:49,479
Then we will hit them at Koyunhisar Plains.

1399
02:11:51,680 --> 02:11:53,479
Let's wait for news first.

1400
02:12:10,640 --> 02:12:12,479
Bora, Bora Bora Bora..

1401
02:12:14,240 --> 02:12:16,759
This road leads to the plains, I know.

1402
02:12:18,280 --> 02:12:20,439
So they are very close.

1403
02:12:21,000 --> 02:12:23,639
-Quickly, let us inform my Bey.
-Stop brother, stop.

1404
02:12:24,040 --> 02:12:26,919
I know the way. You follow these dogs..

1405
02:12:27,160 --> 02:12:28,799
And I will inform Bey.

1406
02:12:29,000 --> 02:12:30,999
-Okay brother, quickly.
-Brother.

1407
02:12:31,080 --> 02:12:33,519
-Be careful.
-Okay brother, quickly now.

1408
02:12:33,640 --> 02:12:35,479
Quickly.

1409
02:12:36,320 --> 02:12:37,679
Quickly.

1410
02:12:44,680 --> 02:12:48,719
After defeating Osman and his Beys at Bafeos Plains..

1411
02:12:49,600 --> 02:12:52,079
The army will continue without resting.

1412
02:12:54,360 --> 02:12:56,199
First Yenisehir.

1413
02:12:56,560 --> 02:12:59,599
Then Inegol, Sogut and Bilecik.

1414
02:13:00,480 --> 02:13:02,559
We will re-take..

1415
02:13:02,720 --> 02:13:05,039
Every place we have lost.

1416
02:13:06,280 --> 02:13:07,799
In Jesus' name..

1417
02:13:08,400 --> 02:13:11,759
We will show no mercy,
no matter who we are facing.

1418
02:13:14,000 --> 02:13:16,079
Let the soldiers be prepared.

1419
02:13:18,680 --> 02:13:20,959
Where is the army, Leo?

1420
02:13:22,360 --> 02:13:24,839
They should've been here by now.

1421
02:13:25,480 --> 02:13:27,959
Send someone immediately.

1422
02:13:33,040 --> 02:13:36,279
We can not wait for the legion coming from the west.

1423
02:13:36,480 --> 02:13:39,599
It is imminent that Osman will know our presence.

1424
02:13:40,360 --> 02:13:42,999
We will move immediately.

1425
02:13:47,920 --> 02:13:49,239
Cerkutay.

1426
02:13:51,080 --> 02:13:52,159
Bey.

1427
02:13:52,320 --> 02:13:55,399
As we have guessed,
they are on the way of Yalakova.

1428
02:13:55,600 --> 02:13:57,399
Bora is onto them.

1429
02:13:57,560 --> 02:14:00,839
Just like that. We are leaving.

1430
02:14:13,800 --> 02:14:16,199
Alps, keep your eyes peeled.

1431
02:14:16,360 --> 02:14:19,079
We may receive news from
the scouts any moment.

1432
02:14:19,240 --> 02:14:20,919
I don't want any flaw.

1433
02:14:20,920 --> 02:14:25,119
Inform the surrounding tribes and tell them
to increase the number of scouts.

1434
02:14:25,120 --> 02:14:28,079
We take precautions
and leave the rest to Allah.

1435
02:14:28,800 --> 02:14:30,559
Yenisehir is our trust.

1436
02:14:30,760 --> 02:14:32,919
Come on, get back to your duties.

1437
02:14:33,000 --> 02:14:35,759
Yes Malhun Hatun!

1438
02:14:39,600 --> 02:14:41,719
Kumral Abdal, what did you do?

1439
02:14:42,120 --> 02:14:43,799
The infirmaries are ready.

1440
02:14:44,400 --> 02:14:47,479
Our deficiencies have been completed, Malhun Hatun.

1441
02:14:48,200 --> 02:14:52,319
I hope we will not need them,
but it is better to take precautions.

1442
02:14:52,320 --> 02:14:54,399
May Allah let them have a safe journey.

1443
02:14:54,400 --> 02:14:56,999
May He not let the enemies
take any opportunity.

1444
02:14:57,080 --> 02:14:58,879
-Ameen.
-I hope so

1445
02:14:59,120 --> 02:15:00,559
I will pray too.

1446
02:15:00,560 --> 02:15:04,279
I will pray so that my father and
others come back safe and sound.

1447
02:15:04,360 --> 02:15:05,519
Pray, of course.

1448
02:15:05,880 --> 02:15:09,519
Allah accept the prayers of children,
my beautiful daughter.

1449
02:15:09,760 --> 02:15:13,559
My Allah, give strength to my father,
he is Osman Bey

1450
02:15:13,880 --> 02:15:18,359
give strength to him,
to my brothers, to his alps.

1451
02:15:18,640 --> 02:15:22,519
Give them power, let them defeat the enemy
and make us happy my Allah.

1452
02:15:22,800 --> 02:15:26,559
Let my father and his army come back
safe and sound,

1453
02:15:26,800 --> 02:15:30,159
let them punish all the evil, aameen.

1454
02:15:30,680 --> 02:15:32,559
-Aameen.
-Aameen.

1455
02:15:32,800 --> 02:15:34,599
Aameen.

1456
02:15:37,720 --> 02:15:39,879
Well done, my beautiful daughter.

1457
02:15:44,800 --> 02:15:46,399
Are the alps ready, Boran?

1458
02:15:46,400 --> 02:15:50,399
All of the alps took up a position my Bey,
they're waiting for your orders.

1459
02:16:37,760 --> 02:16:40,679
There are injured men!

1460
02:16:54,480 --> 02:16:55,718
What's going on?

1461
02:16:57,000 --> 02:16:59,239
Commander

1462
02:17:02,440 --> 02:17:03,759
Osman, sir.

1463
02:17:03,959 --> 02:17:06,879
Osman attacked us, he destroyed our troop.

1464
02:17:11,440 --> 02:17:15,079
Osman! I will drown you with your own blood!

1465
02:17:18,840 --> 02:17:20,999
How did it happen?

1466
02:17:21,360 --> 02:17:22,879
They attacked suddenly, sir.

1467
02:17:23,480 --> 02:17:25,159
There were Turks everywhere.

1468
02:17:25,240 --> 02:17:27,359
We couldn't defend ourselves.

1469
02:17:50,280 --> 02:17:52,279
How did you survive?

1470
02:17:56,840 --> 02:17:59,079
You silly men!

1471
02:17:59,638 --> 02:18:02,919
Osman left you alive to spot our place!

1472
02:18:05,959 --> 02:18:08,558
Osman is here.

1473
02:18:19,879 --> 02:18:21,759
Get the soldiers ready.

1474
02:18:23,160 --> 02:18:25,798
We will drown them all with their own blood!

1475
02:18:29,760 --> 02:18:32,398
Come here Lord.

1476
02:18:33,879 --> 02:18:36,478
This will be your last time.

1477
02:18:45,680 --> 02:18:50,718
We will become a glorious state
after we win this war.

1478
02:18:51,120 --> 02:18:55,079
I swear..
I swear, from now on,

1479
02:18:55,840 --> 02:18:58,239
...we will always attack you!

1480
02:19:11,042 --> 02:19:20,632
Visit our website for more: turkision.com